/* Landfall — the voyage out for any crew (Lachlan, 2026-11-18; DESIGN.md "The voyage out").
   Each of the eighteen voyage cards is built round two officers, and each of their seats has two possible officers, so each card
   has four versions: LF.SOC_ALT[card id][keyA + '+' + keyB] = { title, text, choices: [{ label, note, info, out | ok, bad }] }.
   Text only: the options' tests and effects stay in js/content-social.js and belong to the seat, whoever sits in it. {SUPPER} and
   {WATCH} are the standing first paragraphs. Only the two leads are ever named: the other four seats could hold either officer.
   Written one card at a time, each by a writer given the four officers' sections of VOICES.md. node tools/voices-check.js reads
   every version through. Data only. */
LF.SOC_ALT = {
  "soc.broth": {"estrada+nakamura": {"title": "Lamps and Broth", "text": "Andrea has five in the sick bay who aren't getting better and aren't getting worse: a crushed hand, a bad back, a fever that comes and goes. Samuel has been sitting with them at the end of every shift.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Get them out of here and sit them in the bay under the lamps, where it's warm and smells of something growing. Broth with the greens off the racks. My grandmother kept a ward, and nobody in it stayed in bed.\"\n\n[[nakamura]] \"They're not well enough to move.\" \"I'm glad you sit with them, Samuel, I am. But your bay isn't clean, and I'm not putting a fever in among the greens.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Samuel's way: the lamps and the broth", "ok": "The five sit in a row of chairs between the racks every morning, wrapped up, with a cup of broth each. Inside the month two are back on light work and the fever has gone. Andrea comes up to see it, and stays to help with the pruning.", "bad": "The warmth does them good. The bay doesn't: the fever goes through all five within a few shifts, and the oldest is back in a bed for a month, worse than before. Samuel sits with them every evening until they're up."}, {"label": "The broth, but in the sick bay", "info": [["people", "Samuel, a little"], ["danger", "The five, no quicker"]], "out": "Samuel carries the broth down every evening in a flask. The five are no quicker to mend, but they're cheerful about it, and so is Samuel."}, {"label": "Andrea's sick bay, Andrea's rules", "info": [["people", "Andrea"], ["danger", "Samuel"], ["danger", "The five, still in bed"]], "out": "The five stay where they are. Samuel still comes by at the end of every shift, empty-handed, and sits by the beds anyway."}]}, "waititi+nakamura": {"title": "Lamps and Broth", "text": "Andrea has five in the sick bay who aren't getting better and aren't getting worse: a crushed hand, a bad back, a fever that comes and goes. Hamond has been turning up at the end of every shift with a pot, and the five have started to wait for him.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Get them out of there, my friend, and sit them in the bay under the lamps where it's warm! I'll feed them. There's leek, there's the first of the greens off the racks, there's a stock I've had going that's mostly secret, and nobody has ever been sad in my kitchen, ha!\"\n\n[[nakamura]] \"They're not well enough to move, Hamond.\" \"I'm glad you feed them, I am, but your bay isn't clean, and I'm not putting a fever in among the greens, however good it smells.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Hamond's way: the lamps and the pot", "ok": "The five sit in a row of chairs between the racks every morning, wrapped up, with a bowl each, and Hamond ladles it out himself and tells them what Dalia thinks of leeks. Inside the month two are back on light work and the fever has gone. Andrea comes up to see it, and stays to taste the pot.", "bad": "The warmth does them good. The bay doesn't: the fever goes through all five within a few shifts, and the oldest is back in a bed for a month, worse than before. Hamond carries the pot down to the sick bay every evening and doesn't say a word the whole time, which nobody has ever seen before."}, {"label": "The pot, but in the sick bay", "info": [["people", "Hamond, a little"], ["danger", "The five, no quicker"]], "out": "Hamond carries the pot down every evening with a ladle and an opinion. The five are no quicker to mend, but they're cheerful about it, and so is Hamond, who has promised each of them a different soup."}, {"label": "Andrea's sick bay, Andrea's rules", "info": [["people", "Andrea"], ["danger", "Hamond"], ["danger", "The five, still in bed"]], "out": "The five stay where they are. Hamond still comes by at the end of every shift, and the pot goes into the galley and not to the beds, and he sits by the door with nothing in his hands and nothing to say."}]}, "estrada+brandt": {"title": "Lamps and Broth", "text": "Lou has five in the sick bay who aren't getting better and aren't getting worse: a crushed hand, a bad back, a fever that comes and goes. Samuel has been sitting with them at the end of every shift.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Get them out of here and sit them in the bay under the lamps, where it's warm and smells of something growing. Broth with the greens off the racks. My grandmother kept a ward, and nobody in it stayed in bed.\"\n\n[[brandt]] \"They're not well enough to move.\" \"I'm glad you sit with them, Samuel, it's the only treatment on the ward with no side effects. But your bay isn't clean, and I won't have a fever walking in among the greens because somebody was kind enough to invite it.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Samuel's way: the lamps and the broth", "ok": "The five sit in a row of chairs between the racks every morning, wrapped up, with a cup of broth each. Inside the month two are back on light work and the fever has gone. Lou comes up to see it with a clipboard and no intention of staying, and ends up carrying a crate of pruned stems to the composter without remarking on it.", "bad": "The warmth does them good. The bay doesn't: the fever goes through all five within a few shifts, and the oldest is back in a bed for a month, worse than before. Lou writes it in the book without a word, and is on the ward every evening until they're up, though he'd tell you he happened to be passing."}, {"label": "The broth, but in the sick bay", "info": [["people", "Samuel, a little"], ["danger", "The five, no quicker"]], "out": "Samuel carries the broth down every evening in a flask, and Lou takes the lid off, sniffs it and enters it in the ward notes as a dietary supplement. The five are no quicker to mend, but they're cheerful about it, and so is Samuel."}, {"label": "Lou's sick bay, Lou's rules", "info": [["people", "Lou"], ["danger", "Samuel"], ["danger", "The five, still in bed"]], "out": "The five stay where they are. Samuel still comes by at the end of every shift, empty-handed, and sits by the beds anyway, and Lou moves a chair closer for him without being asked."}]}, "waititi+brandt": {"title": "Lamps and Broth", "text": "Lou has five in the sick bay who aren't getting better and aren't getting worse: a crushed hand, a bad back, a fever that comes and goes. Hamond has been turning up at the end of every shift with a pot, and the five have started to wait for him.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Get them out of there, my friend, and sit them in the bay under the lamps where it's warm! I'll feed them. There's leek, there's the first of the greens off the racks, there's a stock I've had going that's mostly secret, and nobody has ever been sad in my kitchen, ha!\"\n\n[[brandt]] \"They're not well enough to move.\" \"You're not really asking me whether they are. You're asking whether it does any harm to let a man with a ladle feed them, and it doesn't, but your bay isn't clean, and I won't put a fever in among the greens however good the soup smells.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Hamond's way: the lamps and the pot", "ok": "The five sit in a row of chairs between the racks every morning, wrapped up, with a bowl each, and Hamond ladles it out himself and tells them what Dalia thinks of leeks. Inside the month two are back on light work and the fever has gone. Lou comes up to see it, says the soup is a clinical measure, and has two bowls.", "bad": "The warmth does them good. The bay doesn't: the fever goes through all five within a few shifts, and the oldest is back in a bed for a month, worse than before. Lou writes it in the book without a word, and Hamond carries the pot down to the sick bay every evening and doesn't say one either."}, {"label": "The pot, but in the sick bay", "info": [["people", "Hamond, a little"], ["danger", "The five, no quicker"]], "out": "Hamond carries the pot down every evening with a ladle and an opinion, and Lou enters it in the ward notes as a dietary supplement. The five are no quicker to mend, but they're cheerful about it, and so is Hamond, who has promised each of them a different soup."}, {"label": "Lou's sick bay, Lou's rules", "info": [["people", "Lou"], ["danger", "Hamond"], ["danger", "The five, still in bed"]], "out": "The five stay where they are. Hamond still comes by at the end of every shift, and the pot goes into the galley and not to the beds, and he sits by the door with nothing in his hands and nothing to say, until Lou brings him a chair."}]}},
  "soc.coffee": {"kovacs+nakamura": {"title": "The Last Tin", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe real coffee ran out in month nine. Jeremy has found one more tin at the back of an engineering locker, and it's on the table between Jeremy and Andrea, and neither of them has let go of it.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"The night shift in the sick bay hasn't slept in a month, Jeremy.\" \"They're the ones holding people's hands at three in the morning. It's theirs.\"\n\n[[kovacs]] \"The night shift on the reactor hasn't slept in a month either. My locker, my tin.\"\n\nJeremy doesn't let go.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"She's got a temper at three in the morning, the old girl. So have I.\"", "choices": [{"label": "The sick bay's", "info": [["people", "Andrea"], ["danger", "Jeremy"]], "out": "Jeremy lets go of the tin one finger at a time. The sick bay's night shift drinks it a spoon a night for a month and won't hear a word against you. Jeremy brings it up twice more, and not as a joke."}, {"label": "The reactor crew's", "info": [["people", "Jeremy"], ["danger", "Andrea"]], "out": "Jeremy tucks the tin into the overalls and pats it. Andrea says nothing at all, gets up, and takes the bowl back to the sick bay. The reactor crew drinks it for a month and thinks the better of you."}, {"label": "Make it now, here, for the table", "info": [["people", "Everyone at the table"], ["danger", "Gone in one night"]], "out": "Jeremy boils the water and Andrea measures it out like a dose. It's gone in one evening, a cup each. The smell gets into the corridor, and the crew going past stop at the hatch to breathe it."}]}, "halloran+nakamura": {"title": "The Last Tin", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe real coffee ran out in month nine. Roberta has dug one more tin out from behind a coolant manifold in the lander bay, and it's on the table between Roberta and Andrea, and neither of them has let go of it.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"The night shift in the sick bay hasn't slept in a month, Roberta.\" \"They're the ones holding people's hands at three in the morning, and that tin is theirs, so don't make me say it twice.\"\n\n[[halloran]] \"Piss off, Andrea, the reactor's night shift hasn't slept either, and they're up to their elbows in a bastard of a coolant loop! I crawled behind that manifold for it, boss, I got coolant in my fucking hair, and nobody's taking it off me!\"\n\nRoberta hauls the tin against her chest.", "choices": [{"label": "The sick bay's", "info": [["people", "Andrea"], ["danger", "Roberta"]], "out": "Roberta lets go of the tin and swears at the ceiling for a full minute. The sick bay's night shift drinks it a spoon a night for a month and won't hear a word against you. Roberta brings it up twice more, very loudly, and neither time as a joke."}, {"label": "The engineering crew's", "info": [["people", "Roberta"], ["danger", "Andrea"]], "out": "Roberta whoops and kisses the lid. Andrea says nothing at all, gets up, and takes the bowl back to the sick bay. The engineering crew drinks it for a month and thinks the better of you."}, {"label": "Make it now, here, for the table", "info": [["people", "Everyone at the table"], ["danger", "Gone in one night"]], "out": "Roberta insists on doing it properly, with the water weighed out to the gram and the pot scalded first, and Andrea lets her, which is the first thing the two of them have agreed on since the tin turned up. It's gone in one evening, a cup each, and the smell gets into the corridor so that the crew going past stop at the hatch to breathe it."}]}, "kovacs+brandt": {"title": "The Last Tin", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe real coffee ran out in month nine. Jeremy has found one more tin at the back of an engineering locker, and it's on the table between Jeremy and Lou, and Jeremy hasn't let go of it.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Oh, how nice, a tin of coffee and a custody hearing.\" \"The night shift in the sick bay is charting doses on four hours' sleep, Jeremy, which I'd call a clinical argument, although I'll admit it's also a sentimental one, and I'd rather you didn't tell me which of the two is winning.\"\n\n[[kovacs]] \"The night shift on the reactor hasn't slept either, and a tired tech on that deck costs a lot more than a tired nurse. My locker, my tin.\"\n\nJeremy doesn't let go.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"She's got a temper at three in the morning, the old girl. So have I.\"", "choices": [{"label": "The sick bay's", "info": [["people", "Lou"], ["danger", "Jeremy"]], "out": "Jeremy lets go of the tin one finger at a time. Lou writes it into the ward book as a clinical measure and doses it out to the night shift a spoon at a time, and nobody on the ward will hear a word against you. Jeremy brings it up twice more, and not as a joke."}, {"label": "The reactor crew's", "info": [["people", "Jeremy"], ["danger", "Lou"]], "out": "Jeremy tucks the tin into the overalls and pats it. Lou says only that he'll note it in the book, gets up, and goes back to the ward with his cup still empty. The reactor crew drinks it for a month and thinks the better of you."}, {"label": "Make it now, here, for the table", "info": [["people", "Everyone at the table"], ["danger", "Gone in one night"]], "out": "Jeremy boils the water and Lou measures it out like a dose, one cup each and not a drop over, which he calls a prescription. It's gone in one evening, and the smell gets into the corridor, and the crew going past stop at the hatch to breathe it."}]}, "halloran+brandt": {"title": "The Last Tin", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe real coffee ran out in month nine. Roberta has dug one more tin out from behind a coolant manifold in the lander bay, and it's on the table between Roberta and Lou, and Roberta hasn't let go of it.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Oh, how nice, a tin of coffee and a custody hearing.\" \"The night shift in the sick bay is charting doses on four hours' sleep, Roberta, which I'd call a clinical argument, although I'll admit it's also a sentimental one, and I'd rather you didn't tell me which of the two is winning.\"\n\n[[halloran]] \"Piss off, Lou, the reactor's night shift hasn't slept either, and they're up to their elbows in a bastard of a coolant loop! I crawled behind that manifold for it, boss, I got coolant in my fucking hair, and nobody's taking it off me!\"\n\nRoberta hauls the tin against her chest.", "choices": [{"label": "The sick bay's", "info": [["people", "Lou"], ["danger", "Roberta"]], "out": "Roberta lets go of the tin and swears at the ceiling for a full minute. Lou writes it into the ward book as a clinical measure and doses it out to the night shift a spoon at a time, and nobody on the ward will hear a word against you. Roberta brings it up twice more, very loudly, and neither time as a joke."}, {"label": "The engineering crew's", "info": [["people", "Roberta"], ["danger", "Lou"]], "out": "Roberta whoops and kisses the lid. Lou says only that he'll note it in the book, gets up, and goes back to the ward with his cup still empty. The engineering crew drinks it for a month and thinks the better of you."}, {"label": "Make it now, here, for the table", "info": [["people", "Everyone at the table"], ["danger", "Gone in one night"]], "out": "Roberta insists on doing it properly, with the water weighed out to the gram and the pot scalded first, and Lou measures out each cup like a dose and calls it a prescription, and neither of them says a word against the other's method. It's gone in one evening, and the smell gets into the corridor so that the crew going past stop at the hatch to breathe it."}]}},
  "soc.cold": {"solheim+yurbin": {"title": "One More Year", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMac's two years are up at the end of the month, and he doesn't want to go under.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"Years at a time with the instruments running and nobody reading them, think what goes past while I'm asleep, no, think what we're missing right now, let me stay up through the next watch, one more year, and I'll go under after, I promise I'll go under.\"\n\nJane hasn't looked away from the board.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Two years up, then under. That was the rota when you signed it, and it's the rota now.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Jane: two years, then under", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "Mac goes under on the day, with a notebook held against his chest until the lid comes down. Jane signs the log and doesn't say anything about it."}, {"label": "Back Mac: one more year up", "info": [["people", "Mac"], ["yield", "A year of readings"], ["danger", "A third year awake"]], "ok": "Jane gives it a year and not a day more. Mac fills four notebooks with things nobody alive has seen and goes under on the day, grinning, with the notebooks in the pod.", "bad": "A third year awake on a sleeping ship is a long time. By the end Mac is talking to the instruments and sleeping under the big window, and has to be talked into the pod a day at a time."}, {"label": "Ask Mac what it is really", "info": [["people", "Mac"], ["time", "An evening"]], "ok": "It takes a while. Mac is afraid of the lid coming down and never coming up. Jane listens to all of it, then answers.\n\n[[solheim]] \"So am I. Every time.\"\n\nAt the end of the month Jane walks Mac down to the bay herself, and holds his hand until the frost comes.", "bad": "Mac laughs it off, says it's the instruments and only the instruments, and talks about the instruments until morning. You don't get any further, and neither does Jane."}]}, "achebe+yurbin": {"title": "One More Year", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMac's two years are up at the end of the month, and he doesn't want to go under.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"Years at a time with the instruments running and nobody reading them, think what goes past while I'm asleep, no, think what we're missing right now, let me stay up through the next watch, one more year, and I'll go under after, I promise I'll go under.\"\n\nLucas lets him get all the way to the end.\n\n[[achebe]] \"Listen, Mac, I've heard you, and I'm not saying it lightly. Two years up and then under is what you signed, and it's what the folks in the cold already did for us, and I don't want to be the one who bends it for the man who asks nicely. So tell me why it matters, and I'll tell you where I land.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Lucas: two years, then under", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "Mac goes under on the day, with a notebook held against his chest until the lid comes down. Lucas signs the log, and stays at the bay a while after the frost has come."}, {"label": "Back Mac: one more year up", "info": [["people", "Mac"], ["yield", "A year of readings"], ["danger", "A third year awake"]], "ok": "Lucas gives it a year, says it twice so there's no mistaking it, and means it both times. Mac fills four notebooks with things nobody alive has seen and goes under on the day, grinning, with the notebooks in the pod.", "bad": "A third year awake on a sleeping ship is a long time. By the end Mac is talking to the instruments and sleeping under the big window, and Lucas has to talk him into the pod a day at a time."}, {"label": "Ask Mac what it is really", "info": [["people", "Mac"], ["time", "An evening"]], "ok": "It takes a while. Mac is afraid of the lid coming down and never coming up. Lucas doesn't hurry him, and when it's all said he tells Mac he's never liked it either, and that's nothing to be ashamed of. At the end of the month Lucas walks Mac down to the bay himself, and stays with him until the frost comes.", "bad": "Mac laughs it off, says it's the instruments and only the instruments, and talks about the instruments until morning. Lucas asks him once more, plainly, and then lets it go. You don't get any further, and neither does he."}]}, "solheim+iyer": {"title": "One More Year", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMichelle's two years are up at the end of the month, and she'd like to stay awake.\n\n[[iyer]] \"I would ask to remain on the watch for a further year, Administrator, provided the rota can bear it, since the baseline we've built would then run unbroken to the end of the crossing and not be left to whoever wakes to read it, which would be a good deal less useful to you at landfall than I could make it. I'd put the cost to my own health at something I'm prepared to pay.\"\n\nJane hasn't looked away from the board.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Two years up, then under. That was the rota when you signed it, Michelle, and it's the rota now.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Jane: two years, then under", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "Michelle goes under on the day, with a slate of her figures held against her chest until the lid comes down. Jane signs the log and doesn't say anything about it."}, {"label": "Back Michelle: one more year up", "info": [["people", "Michelle"], ["yield", "An unbroken baseline"], ["danger", "A third year awake"]], "ok": "Jane gives it a year and not a day more. Michelle fills the log with a baseline nobody else could have kept and goes under on the day, entirely composed, with the whole record in the pod beside her.", "bad": "A third year awake on a sleeping ship is a long time. By the end Michelle has stopped keeping any hours but the instruments', and has to be walked to the pod, with her figures read out to her, a day at a time."}, {"label": "Ask Michelle what it is really", "info": [["people", "Michelle"], ["time", "An evening"]], "ok": "It takes a while, and what comes out is arithmetic.\n\n[[iyer]] \"The last sleep cost me a month of fine work on waking, Administrator, and I've no way to say what the next will take.\"\n\nJane listens to all of it, then answers.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Write down what you've got in hand before the lid goes. I'll make sure it's read.\"\n\nAt the end of the month Jane walks Michelle down to the bay herself, and checks the seal before she leaves.", "bad": "Michelle gives a complete and accurate account of the instruments, and an equally accurate account of why the instruments are the whole of it. You don't get any further, and neither does Jane."}]}, "achebe+iyer": {"title": "One More Year", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMichelle's two years are up at the end of the month, and she'd like to stay awake.\n\n[[iyer]] \"I would ask to remain on the watch for a further year, Administrator, provided the rota can bear it, since the baseline we've built would then run unbroken to the end of the crossing and not be left to whoever wakes to read it, which would be a good deal less useful to you at landfall than I could make it. I'd put the cost to my own health at something I'm prepared to pay.\"\n\nLucas waits until she has finished.\n\n[[achebe]] \"Michelle, I've heard you out, and I think you've told me the truth about what you want. Two years up and then under is what you signed, and it's what everybody in the cold already did for us. I won't call it a small thing to ask. Before I say anything else, tell me the cost like you'd tell it to a friend, and then I'll tell you where I land.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Lucas: two years, then under", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "Michelle goes under on the day, with a slate of her figures held against her chest until the lid comes down. Lucas signs the log, and stays at the bay a while after the frost has come."}, {"label": "Back Michelle: one more year up", "info": [["people", "Michelle"], ["yield", "An unbroken baseline"], ["danger", "A third year awake"]], "ok": "Lucas gives it a year, says it twice so there's no mistaking it, and means it both times. Michelle fills the log with a baseline nobody else could have kept and goes under on the day, entirely composed, with the whole record in the pod beside her.", "bad": "A third year awake on a sleeping ship is a long time. By the end Michelle has stopped keeping any hours but the instruments', and Lucas has to walk her to the pod with her own figures read out to her, a day at a time."}, {"label": "Ask Michelle what it is really", "info": [["people", "Michelle"], ["time", "An evening"]], "ok": "It takes a while, and what comes out is arithmetic.\n\n[[iyer]] \"The last sleep cost me a month of fine work on waking, Administrator, and I've no way to say what the next will take.\"\n\nLucas doesn't try to argue her out of it. He tells her it's a fair thing to count, and that it's all right to count it out loud. At the end of the month Lucas walks Michelle down to the bay himself, and stays until the frost comes.", "bad": "Michelle gives a complete and accurate account of the instruments, and an equally accurate account of why the instruments are the whole of it. Lucas asks her once more, plainly, and then lets it go. You don't get any further, and neither does he."}]}},
  "soc.count": {"nakamura+solheim": {"title": "Jane's Book", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nAndrea has found Jane's notebook, the one nobody else sees. It has nine lines in it, one for every death since the burn: the pods that failed in the first year, the rigger crushed in the spine, each with a name. Jane is standing with a hand out for it.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"The others should hear it.\" \"Wake them for one supper and read it out loud, all of it. They're not yours to carry, Jane.\"\n\nJane speaks very quietly.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Give it back.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Andrea: wake the others for one supper, and read it out", "ok": "Jane takes the notebook back and looks at it a long time.\n\n[[solheim]] \"One supper, then. I'll read it.\"\n\nThe four are brought up out of the cold for a night, and Jane reads all nine without stopping. Andrea is crying by the end of it, and Jane looks ten years lighter.", "bad": "Jane takes the notebook, puts it inside the flight jacket and leaves the flight deck without a word. The next morning there's a new lock on Jane's locker. Andrea tells you you've made it worse, and is probably right."}, {"label": "Back Jane: it's Jane's to carry", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Andrea"], ["danger", "What Jane carries"]], "out": "Andrea hands it back. Jane puts it away and speaks to you, not to Andrea.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Thank you.\"\n\nAndrea doesn't speak to either of you for the rest of the watch."}, {"label": "Ask Jane to read you one", "ok": "Jane opens it at the first page and reads one name. Andrea knew them, as it turns out, and tells you about them. Then Jane reads another. By ship's morning they've done all nine, and Jane is the one turning the pages.", "bad": "Jane reads them all, in order, flat, and then reads them again and doesn't stop when Andrea asks. Neither of them looks at you when the lamps come up."}]}, "brandt+solheim": {"title": "Jane's Book", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nJane's notebook has slid out of her jacket where it hangs over the back of a chair, and Lou has picked it up and read it before anyone could say a word. It has nine lines in it, one for every death since the burn: the pods that failed in the first year, the rigger crushed in the spine, each with a name. Jane is standing with a hand out for it.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Nine names, Jane, kept by one person for years with nobody to say them to, which is a condition with a known course.\" \"Wake the others for one supper and have it read out loud, because I don't expect it to improve by itself.\"\n\nJane speaks very quietly.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Give it back.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Lou: wake the others for one supper, and read it out", "ok": "Jane takes the notebook back and looks at it a long time.\n\n[[solheim]] \"One supper, then. I'll read it.\"\n\nThe four are brought up out of the cold for a night, and Jane reads all nine without stopping. Lou says nothing at all through the last name, which for Lou is a great deal, and Jane looks ten years lighter.", "bad": "Jane takes the notebook, puts it inside the flight jacket and leaves the flight deck without a word. The next morning there's a new lock on Jane's locker. Lou tells you he did say it would go this way, and that he'd have preferred to be wrong."}, {"label": "Back Jane: it's Jane's to carry", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Lou"], ["danger", "What Jane carries"]], "out": "Lou hands it back. Jane puts it away and speaks to you, not to Lou.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Thank you.\"\n\nLou says he'd like it noted that he advised otherwise, and after that he speaks to neither of you except to ask for the sugar."}, {"label": "Ask Jane to read you one", "ok": "Jane opens it at the first page and reads one name. Lou treated the rigger in the yard clinic, as it turns out, and tells you what the man was like in the chair. Then Jane reads another. By ship's morning they've done all nine, and Jane is the one turning the pages.", "bad": "Jane reads them all, in order, flat, and then reads them again. Lou stops her once, and then once more.\n\n[[brandt]] \"That will do, Jane.\"\n\nShe goes on. Neither of them looks at you when the lamps come up."}]}, "nakamura+achebe": {"title": "Lucas's Book", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nAndrea has found Lucas's notebook, the one nobody else sees. It has nine names in it, one for every death since the burn: the pods that failed in the first year, the rigger crushed in the spine, and under each name a line about who that person was. Lucas is standing with a hand out for it.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"Lucas, the others knew these people too, and they ought to hear it from you.\" \"Wake them for one supper and read it out loud, every name, because you shouldn't be the only one holding them.\"\n\nLucas speaks gently.\n\n[[achebe]] \"Listen, Andrea, I know why you want it, and I'd still like it back.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Andrea: wake the others for one supper, and read it out", "ok": "Lucas takes the notebook back and looks at it a long time.\n\n[[achebe]] \"All right. One supper, and I'll read it, because I'd rather they heard it from me than found out.\"\n\nThe four are brought up out of the cold for a night, and Lucas reads all nine, a line about each, and stops twice. Andrea is crying by the end of it, and Lucas looks ten years lighter.", "bad": "Lucas takes the notebook and puts it inside his jacket.\n\n[[achebe]] \"I expected we'd talk about this first, you and I.\"\n\nThe next morning he's polite to you, and busy, and doesn't meet your eye. Andrea tells you you've made it worse, and is probably right."}, {"label": "Back Lucas: it's Lucas's to carry", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Andrea"], ["danger", "What Lucas carries"]], "out": "Andrea hands it back. Lucas puts it away and speaks to you, and then to her.\n\n[[achebe]] \"Thank you.\" \"I'm sorry, Andrea.\"\n\nShe doesn't answer. She doesn't speak to either of you for the rest of the watch."}, {"label": "Ask Lucas to read you one", "ok": "Lucas opens it at the first page and reads one name and the line under it. Andrea knew them, as it turns out, and tells you about them. Then Lucas reads another. By ship's morning they've done all nine, and Lucas is the one turning the pages.", "bad": "Lucas reads them all, in order, and then goes back to the first and starts again, and doesn't stop when Andrea asks him to. Neither of them looks at you when the lamps come up."}]}, "brandt+achebe": {"title": "Lucas's Book", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nLou has picked up Lucas's notebook from the console, where it was left open, and read it before anyone could say a word. It has nine names in it, one for every death since the burn: the pods that failed in the first year, the rigger crushed in the spine, and under each name a line about who that person was. Lucas is standing with a hand out for it.\n\n[[brandt]] \"You've written what each of them was like, Lucas, which tells me you're not keeping a count, you're keeping a vigil, and a vigil kept alone has a poor prognosis.\" \"Wake the others for one supper and read it out loud.\"\n\nLucas speaks gently.\n\n[[achebe]] \"Listen, Lou, I know why you want it, and I'd still like it back.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Lou: wake the others for one supper, and read it out", "ok": "Lucas takes the notebook back and looks at it a long time.\n\n[[achebe]] \"All right. One supper, and I'll read it, because I'd rather they heard it from me than found out.\"\n\nThe four are brought up out of the cold for a night, and Lucas reads all nine, a line about each, and stops twice. Lou says nothing through the last name, which for Lou is a great deal, and Lucas looks ten years lighter.", "bad": "Lucas takes the notebook and puts it inside his jacket.\n\n[[achebe]] \"I expected we'd talk about this first, you and I.\"\n\nThe next morning he's polite to you, and busy, and doesn't meet your eye. Lou tells you he did say it would go this way, and that he'd have preferred to be wrong."}, {"label": "Back Lucas: it's Lucas's to carry", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Lou"], ["danger", "What Lucas carries"]], "out": "Lou hands it back. Lucas puts it away and speaks to you, and then to Lou.\n\n[[achebe]] \"Thank you.\" \"I'm sorry, Lou.\"\n\nLou lets it go by. After that Lucas speaks to neither of you except to ask for the sugar."}, {"label": "Ask Lucas to read you one", "ok": "Lucas opens it at the first page and reads one name and the line under it. Lou treated the rigger in the yard clinic, as it turns out, and tells you what the man was like in the chair. Then Lucas reads another. By ship's morning they've done all nine, and Lucas is the one turning the pages.", "bad": "Lucas reads them all, in order, and then goes back to the first and starts again. Lou stops him once, and then once more.\n\n[[brandt]] \"That will do, Lucas.\"\n\nHe goes on. Neither of them looks at you when the lamps come up."}]}},
  "soc.door": {"kovacs+solheim": {"title": "Half a Door", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nJane and Jeremy flew together before the ship, and Jeremy has decided the table should know it.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Kiruna, the old test field. Jane brings a lander in sideways and takes the hangar door clean off. The whole door, and guess who hung the new one.\"\n\n[[solheim]] \"Half a door, in a forty-knot crosswind.\"\n\nJane doesn't stop eating.\n\n[[solheim]] \"You rebuilt the other half crooked, and it was still crooked when we left, because I checked.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Laugh at Jeremy's story", "info": [["people", "Jeremy"], ["danger", "Jane, who doesn't like being the joke"]], "out": "Jeremy is delighted, and tells it twice more, with the door bigger each time. Jane lets it go, but you see it noted."}, {"label": "Laugh at Jane's", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Jeremy, a little"]], "out": "Jeremy laughs hardest of anyone and swears the door was straight. Jane almost smiles. It's the first time anyone at the table has seen it."}, {"label": "Ask what flying was like, back then", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "Jane doesn't talk about it"]], "out": "Jane gives a one-word answer and goes back to the stew. Jeremy fills in the rest: night landings, a dead engine over the sea, how Jane got them both home. Jane doesn't correct a word of it. They're still at the table when the lamp is turned down."}]}, "halloran+solheim": {"title": "Half a Door", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nJane and Roberta flew together before the ship, and Roberta has had two glasses of the still's best and decided the table should know it.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Kiruna, the old test field! Jane brings a lander in sideways and takes the whole fucking hangar door off, and who hangs the new one? Me, boss, that's who! Hinges to gauge, every bolt torqued, and it swung like a dream!\"\n\n[[solheim]] \"Half a door, in a forty-knot crosswind.\"\n\nJane doesn't stop eating.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Your hinge pins were the wrong grade, so the door sagged inside a month, and I put it in the report.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Laugh at Roberta's story", "info": [["people", "Roberta"], ["danger", "Jane, who doesn't like being the joke"]], "out": "Roberta is delighted and tells it twice more, swearing at the door harder each time. Jane lets it go, but you see it noted."}, {"label": "Laugh at Jane's", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Roberta, a little"]], "out": "Roberta roars, shouts that the pins were the only ones in the stores, and throws a bread roll at the report. Jane almost smiles. It's the first time anyone at the table has seen it."}, {"label": "Ask what flying was like, back then", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "Jane doesn't talk about it"]], "out": "Jane gives a one-word answer and goes back to the stew. Roberta fills in the rest, loudly: night landings, a dead engine over the sea, how Jane got them both home. Jane doesn't correct a word of it. They're still at the table when the lamp is turned down."}]}, "kovacs+achebe": {"title": "The Left-Handed Spanner", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nLucas and Jeremy served on the same hull before the Ariadne, and Jeremy has decided the table should hear how it started.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"First week he's aboard, Lucas comes down to my plant and asks what the most important tool in the shop is. I told him a left-handed spanner and sent him up three decks to borrow one. He was gone the best part of an hour.\"\n\n[[achebe]] \"Listen, I asked every soul on those three decks, Jeremy, and not one of them told me.\"\n\nLucas laughs, and then looks at him.\n\n[[achebe]] \"That one was a long walk, and I've not forgiven the engine room yet.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Laugh at Jeremy's story", "info": [["people", "Jeremy"], ["danger", "Lucas, a little"]], "out": "Jeremy is delighted, and tells it twice more, with the decks getting taller each time. Lucas takes it well, but you notice he stops asking the engine room what it needs."}, {"label": "Laugh at Lucas's", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Jeremy, a little"]], "out": "Lucas tells the rest of it himself, how a deck cook finally handed him a mug of tea and a straight answer. Jeremy grunts and swears the old hands did it to every officer. Lucas says he knows, and that he's done it since, once."}, {"label": "Ask what the hull was like, back then", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "Jeremy doesn't talk about it"]], "out": "Jeremy gives a one-word answer and goes back to the stew. Lucas fills in the rest, in his slow way: the old plant, the crew who stayed through the bad winter, what Jeremy did to keep her turning. Jeremy doesn't correct a word of it. They're still at the table when the lamp is turned down."}]}, "halloran+achebe": {"title": "Up to His Chest", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nLucas and Roberta served on the same hull before the Ariadne, and Roberta has had two glasses of the still's best and decided the table should hear how it started.\n\n[[halloran]] \"First week he's aboard, Lucas volunteers for the tank bay, boss! Nice man, new boots, wants to help! I hand him a hose and say mind the grey water, and the daft bastard walks straight into it up to his chest!\"\n\n[[achebe]] \"Listen, I asked you what the smell was, Roberta, and you told me it was fine.\"\n\nLucas is laughing, and he's shaking his head.\n\n[[achebe]] \"That one was yours, and I wore those boots for a month because I couldn't get the stink out.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Laugh at Roberta's story", "info": [["people", "Roberta"], ["danger", "Lucas, a little"]], "out": "Roberta is delighted, and tells it twice more, with the water higher each time. Lucas takes it well, but he asks quietly who has been down to the tank bay lately."}, {"label": "Laugh at Lucas's", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Roberta, a little"]], "out": "Lucas tells the rest of it himself, how the cook hosed him down on the loading dock and the whole bay watched. Roberta shouts that she brought him a towel, which is true, and that she's never been so proud of anyone."}, {"label": "Ask what the hull was like, back then", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "Roberta doesn't talk about it"]], "out": "Roberta says it was a heap of shit and goes back to the stew. Lucas fills in the rest, in his slow way: the crew who stayed through the bad winter, and the night Roberta rebuilt a pump by hand because nobody else would. Roberta doesn't correct a word of it. They're still at the table when the lamp is turned down."}]}},
  "soc.dressing": {"nakamura+dahl": {"title": "Field Dressing", "text": "Andrea wants to teach Nolan's security detail to pack a wound and tie off a bleed: two shifts a month, off their rounds.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"Somebody's going to get hurt in the spine one day, and it'll be your lot carrying them to me.\"\n\nNolan has a long history with Andrea's needle, from before the ship, and a scar through one eyebrow to show for it.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Two shifts off the rounds. Lovely. And who walks the cryo decks while they're learning knots?\"", "choices": [{"label": "Andrea's shifts", "ok": "The detail learns it, grumbling, on each other's arms. Before the year is out one of them packs a gash in a rigger's thigh out in the spine, and the rigger walks into the sick bay on two feet. Nolan tells it at supper as if the detail thought of it.", "bad": "On the second shift, with half the detail in the sick bay, somebody gets into the dry stores and a whole pallet of rations walks off and is never seen again. Nolan stands in the empty bay and says one word, as if it were a curse.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Knots.\"\n\nHe says nothing else for a day."}, {"label": "The rounds first. Andrea teaches whoever comes in their own time", "info": [["people", "Nolan"], ["danger", "Andrea"]], "out": "Four of the detail come to the sick bay on their rest days. Nolan isn't one of them, and says so. Andrea teaches the four anyway and tells you, twice, that four isn't enough."}, {"label": "Nolan first, alone, so the detail sees it", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "Nolan's pride"]], "out": "Nolan sits at Andrea's table for an evening being shown how to tie off an arm, and doesn't make a single joke. Halfway through Andrea brings up the eyebrow and the night it was stitched, and Nolan laughs out loud. The detail signs up the next morning."}]}, "brandt+dahl": {"title": "Field Dressing", "text": "Lou wants Nolan's security detail taught to pack a wound and tie off a bleed: two shifts a month, off their rounds.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Somebody on your detail is going to put a tourniquet on the wrong end of a man one day, and I'd rather spend two shifts on it now than a night on it afterwards.\"\n\nNolan has a long history with Lou's bedside manner, from before the ship, and has never forgiven being told what was wrong with him before the scan came back.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Two shifts off the rounds, and the doctor's very sure it's for our benefit, which is touching, and who walks the cryo decks while my lot are practising on each other's arms, since I'd like to know which of us he thinks is being looked after?\"", "choices": [{"label": "Lou's shifts", "ok": "The detail learns it, grumbling, on each other's arms. Before the year is out one of them packs a gash in a rigger's thigh out in the spine, and the rigger walks into the sick bay on two feet. Lou says the packing was adequate, which from him is a medal, and Nolan tells it at supper as if the detail thought of it.", "bad": "On the second shift, with half the detail in the sick bay, somebody gets into the dry stores and a whole pallet of rations walks off and is never seen again. Nolan stands in the empty bay and speaks quietly.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Doctor's orders.\"\n\nHe says nothing else for a day."}, {"label": "The rounds first. Lou teaches whoever comes in their own time", "info": [["people", "Nolan"], ["danger", "Lou"]], "out": "Four of the detail come to the sick bay on their rest days. Nolan isn't one of them, and says so. Lou teaches the four anyway and tells you, once, that you're not really asking whether four is enough, you're asking whether you can stop thinking about it."}, {"label": "Nolan first, alone, so the detail sees it", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "Nolan's pride"]], "out": "Nolan sits at Lou's table for an evening being shown how to tie off an arm, and doesn't make a single joke. Halfway through Lou tells him he's not suspicious of the lesson, he's suspicious of being helped, and Nolan laughs out loud and admits it. The detail signs up the next morning."}]}, "nakamura+zulu": {"title": "Field Dressing", "text": "Andrea wants to teach Toby's watch to pack a wound and tie off a bleed: two shifts a month, off their posts.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"Somebody's going to bleed in the spine one day, Toby, and it'll be one of yours on the end of the stretcher, so I'd like them to know what to do with their hands before it happens.\"\n\nToby has been standing in her sick bay for ten minutes with his cap in his hand.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, two shifts a month is two shifts the cryo decks are short, and I'd ask who walks them, because I won't leave a post of mine with one person on it. I'd also like it noted that I think she's right.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Andrea's shifts", "ok": "The watch learns it, politely, on each other's arms, and Toby learns it first and best. Before the year is out one of them packs a gash in a rigger's thigh out in the spine, and the rigger walks into the sick bay on two feet. Toby reports it in order, with the names, and Andrea has to look away.", "bad": "On the second shift, with half the watch in the sick bay, somebody gets into the dry stores and a whole pallet of rations walks off and is never seen again. Toby comes to you before anyone asks.\n\n[[zulu]] \"That was my rota and my post, and I'd like it written down that way.\"\n\nHe doesn't say much else for a day."}, {"label": "The posts first. Andrea teaches whoever comes in their own time", "info": [["people", "Toby"], ["danger", "Andrea"]], "out": "Four of the watch come to the sick bay on their rest days. Toby isn't one of them, and apologises for it twice, because the posts were short again. Andrea teaches the four anyway and tells you, loudly, that four isn't enough."}, {"label": "Toby first, alone, so the watch sees it", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "The cryo decks, short for an evening"]], "out": "Toby sits at Andrea's table for an evening being shown how to tie off an arm, and gets every knot right and apologises for each one that takes him twice. Halfway through Andrea tells him about the first patient she lost, and Toby puts the bandage down and listens with his whole face. The watch signs up the next morning."}]}, "brandt+zulu": {"title": "Field Dressing", "text": "Lou wants Toby's watch taught to pack a wound and tie off a bleed: two shifts a month, off their posts.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Your people are the ones who'll find the injured first, so they may as well be the ones who don't make it worse. That's a clinical argument, whatever your face is telling me about it.\"\n\nToby has been standing in the sick bay for ten minutes with his cap in his hand.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Doctor, two shifts a month is two shifts the cryo decks are short, and I'd ask who walks them, because I won't leave a post of mine with one person on it. I'd also like it noted that you're right.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Lou's shifts", "ok": "The watch learns it, politely, on each other's arms, and Toby learns it first and best. Before the year is out one of them packs a gash in a rigger's thigh out in the spine, and the rigger walks into the sick bay on two feet. Lou says it was acceptable, and then sits up with the rigger anyway, though he'd tell you he was passing.", "bad": "On the second shift, with half the watch in the sick bay, somebody gets into the dry stores and a whole pallet of rations walks off and is never seen again. Toby comes to you before anyone asks.\n\n[[zulu]] \"That was my rota and my post, and I'd like it written down that way.\"\n\nHe doesn't say much else for a day."}, {"label": "The posts first. Lou teaches whoever comes in their own time", "info": [["people", "Toby"], ["danger", "Lou"]], "out": "Four of the watch come to the sick bay on their rest days. Toby isn't one of them, and apologises for it twice, because the posts were short again. Lou teaches the four anyway and tells you that four is a poor prognosis, in the tone of a man reading out the weather."}, {"label": "Toby first, alone, so the watch sees it", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "The cryo decks, short for an evening"]], "out": "Toby sits at Lou's table for an evening being shown how to tie off an arm, and gets every knot right and apologises for each one that takes him twice. Halfway through Lou tells him that he isn't worried about the knots, he's worried about the people who'll be on the other end of them, and Toby thanks him gravely, as if it were an order. The watch signs up the next morning."}]}},
  "soc.grace": {"dahl+estrada": {"title": "Grace", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nSamuel waits until everyone has a bowl, then bows over his and says a grace, low, in the old words. Someone down the table waits with the spoon in the air.\n\nNolan doesn't.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Who's listening out here, Samuel? We left the last church behind at Mars, and the only thing in this room that answers to anybody is the stew.\"\n\nSamuel doesn't look up.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Far enough out you'd need to say it loud, so I do.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Bow your head with Samuel", "info": [["people", "Samuel"], ["danger", "Nolan, left holding the spoon"]], "out": "You bow your head, and so does the rest of the table. Nolan puts the spoon down and waits, which is more than anyone expected. Samuel finishes.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Eat.\"\n\nHe smiles at you for the first time since the burn."}, {"label": "Laugh at Nolan's line", "info": [["people", "Nolan"], ["danger", "Samuel"]], "out": "Nolan grins and starts eating. Samuel finishes the grace anyway, more quietly, and doesn't say much else at the table that night."}, {"label": "Ask Samuel to add a word for the ones left on Earth", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "A quiet table"]], "out": "Samuel does, without missing a beat. Nobody laughs at that one. Nolan's head goes down with the rest and stays down a little longer than Samuel's, and nobody says much for the rest of the meal."}]}, "zulu+estrada": {"title": "Grace", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nSamuel waits until everyone has a bowl, then bows over his and says a grace, low, in the old words. Toby hasn't sat. He is standing at the end of the table with his tray, looking at the clock over the hatch.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Samuel, my relief is due on the flight deck in ten minutes, and I won't have them standing my watch for me, so I'd ask if the grace might be short tonight. I'm sorry, I know it isn't mine to ask.\"\n\nSamuel doesn't look up.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Far enough out you'd need to say it loud, so I do. It's as long as it is.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Bow your head with Samuel", "info": [["people", "Samuel"], ["danger", "Toby's relief, waiting"]], "out": "You bow your head, and so does the rest of the table. Toby bows too, on his feet, with the tray held in both hands, and goes to his post late. Samuel finishes.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Eat.\"\n\nHe smiles at you for the first time since the burn."}, {"label": "Back Toby's watch", "info": [["people", "Toby"], ["danger", "Samuel"]], "out": "You tell Samuel the relief has to go on time, and Toby thanks you twice, correctly, and is out of the hatch before the first spoon. Samuel finishes the grace anyway, more quietly, and doesn't say much else at the table that night."}, {"label": "Ask Samuel to add a word for the ones on watch", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "A quiet table"]], "out": "Samuel does, without missing a beat, and names the flight deck and the dark outside it. Nobody laughs at that one. Toby's head goes down with the rest and stays down a little longer than Samuel's, and he is two minutes late to his relief and doesn't mention it."}]}, "dahl+waititi": {"title": "Grace", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nHamond waits until everyone has a bowl, then stands, which nobody asked him to, and says a grace. It starts with the beans in the stew, wanders by way of his mother's kitchen and his uncle Tarek's goat, and arrives at Dalia asleep in the cryo banks, who would be telling him to sit down. The stew has stopped steaming.\n\nNolan hasn't touched his spoon.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Who's listening out here, Hamond? We left the last church behind at Mars, and I notice you've thanked every cook you ever had and not once the people who'd like to eat before it's bloody cold.\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"Ha! It's not cold, my friend, it's resting! And somebody's listening, somebody always is, and if it's only Dalia through the glass, she's heard worse from me.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Bow your head with Hamond", "info": [["people", "Hamond"], ["danger", "Nolan, left holding the spoon"]], "out": "You bow your head, and so does the rest of the table. Nolan puts the spoon down and waits, which is more than anyone expected. Hamond finishes at last.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Eat! Eat, my friend!\"\n\nHe claps you on the shoulder hard enough to slop your bowl."}, {"label": "Laugh at Nolan's line", "info": [["people", "Nolan"], ["danger", "Hamond"]], "out": "Nolan grins and starts eating. Hamond finishes the grace anyway, much shorter, and for once tells no story over the meal."}, {"label": "Ask Hamond to add a word for the ones in the cryo banks", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "A quiet table"]], "out": "Hamond does, and the booming stops. He goes plain and short and says their names, Dalia's last. Nobody laughs at that one. Nolan's head goes down with the rest and stays down a little longer than Hamond's, and nobody says much for the rest of the meal."}]}, "zulu+waititi": {"title": "One Loaf", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nHamond has been in the galley since morning and has let nobody in. He comes out with a loaf, a real one, risen and brown, and sets it in the middle of the table like a baby. Then he stands and says a grace over it that takes in the flour, his mother and a promise that every supper from here to landfall will have one.\n\nToby has waited out the whole of it with his hands folded.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Hamond, that loaf is a good part of a week's flour, and I've read the stores list. I'd ask that we count before we promise, because my people will remember a promise.\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"He's counting, my friend, at my table! Ha!\"\n\nHamond is still smiling, but he hasn't looked up from the bread.\n\n[[waititi]] \"I know, I know, I said it with my whole chest, and I'd say it again.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Break the bread with Hamond", "info": [["people", "Hamond"], ["danger", "Toby, left holding his plate"]], "out": "You tear the first piece off, and so does the rest of the table. Toby takes his slice in both hands and eats it as though he were apologising to it.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Eat!\"\n\nHamond beams at you for the first time since the burn."}, {"label": "Take Toby's side", "info": [["people", "Toby"], ["danger", "Hamond"]], "out": "You say the count comes first, and Toby thanks you, correctly. Hamond cuts the loaf into thin slices anyway, more quietly than anyone has seen him do anything, and tells no story over the meal."}, {"label": "Ask Hamond to set a slice aside for the watch below", "info": [["people", "Both of them"], ["danger", "A quiet table"]], "out": "Hamond does, and wraps it in a cloth, and Toby watches it go with his chin up. Nobody laughs at that one. Toby carries the parcel down to the flight deck himself and writes the loaf into the log as a gift, to be safe, and nobody says much for the rest of the meal."}]}},
  "soc.jar": {"dahl+yurbin": {"title": "Something in a Jar", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nMac has brought a jar to supper and put it down beside the salt. Something no bigger than a grain of rice is swimming in it, thousands of them. Someone looks at it once and goes on eating.\n\nNolan holds it up to the lamp.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Lovely. Dinner and a specimen. Does it eat stew, or does it eat us?\"\n\n[[yurbin]] \"Tardigrades! Out of the soil cores, and no, Nolan, they don't eat stew, they don't eat anything, they dry themselves out and wait, which is, hold on, look at that one, it's moving, they'll outlive the ship, they'll outlive all of us.\"\n\nMac takes the jar back.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"Shame they don't do security, they'd be better at it.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Laugh at Nolan's", "info": [["people", "Nolan"], ["danger", "Mac's pride"]], "out": "Nolan grins and passes you the bread. Mac puts the jar in a vest pocket and eats the rest of the meal without a word, which for Mac is a long time."}, {"label": "Laugh at Mac's", "info": [["people", "Mac"], ["danger", "Nolan, outnumbered"]], "out": "[[dahl]] \"Fair.\" \"Beaten by a jar, and it didn't even have to try.\"\n\nNolan means it. Mac is so pleased that the jar goes round the whole table, and Nolan holds it up to the lamp for longer than anyone."}, {"label": "Ask Mac what they are", "note": "Mac will tell you. All of it.", "info": [["yield", "Something learned"], ["danger", "Nolan's supper"]], "out": "Mac talks until the stew is cold: how they dry out and wait, how long they can wait, what they can wait through. Nolan gets up halfway through to walk the cryo decks and leaves the plate. You come away knowing more about water bears than anyone ought to."}]}, "zulu+yurbin": {"title": "Something in a Jar", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nMac has brought a jar to supper and put it down beside the salt. Something no bigger than a grain of rice is swimming in it, thousands of them. Someone looks at it once and goes on eating.\n\nToby has not touched his bowl.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Mac, I'd ask that you take that back to the lab before we eat, because the galley is mine to keep clean, and nobody has told me what's in the jar.\"\n\n[[yurbin]] \"Tardigrades! Out of the soil cores, and they're nothing, Toby, honestly, they don't eat anything, they dry themselves out and wait, which is, hold on, look at that one, it's moving, they'll outlive the ship, they'll outlive all of us.\"\n\nMac turns the jar to the lamp and then, a little late, to you.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"I should've asked. But look at it.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Back Toby", "info": [["people", "Toby"], ["danger", "Mac's pride"]], "out": "You tell Mac the jar goes back to the lab, and Toby thanks you and means it, and asks quietly whether Mac would like him to carry it down. Mac puts it in a vest pocket and eats the rest of the meal without a word, which for Mac is a long time."}, {"label": "Back Mac", "info": [["people", "Mac"], ["danger", "Toby, outnumbered"]], "out": "[[zulu]] \"Understood.\" \"I'm sorry, Mac, I made a fuss over a jar.\"\n\nMac is so pleased that the jar goes round the whole table, and Toby holds it up to the lamp for longer than anyone and asks how you would tell if one of them had died."}, {"label": "Ask Mac what they are", "note": "Mac will tell you. All of it.", "info": [["yield", "Something learned"], ["danger", "Toby's supper"]], "out": "Mac talks until the stew is cold: how they dry out and wait, how long they can wait, what they can wait through. Toby listens politely to most of it, then excuses himself because it's the hour of his rounds, and the plate stays where it is. You come away knowing more about water bears than anyone ought to."}]}, "dahl+iyer": {"title": "Something in a Jar", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nMichelle has brought a jar to supper and set it down beside the salt. Something no bigger than a grain of rice is swimming in it, thousands of them. Someone looks at it once and goes on eating.\n\nNolan holds it up to the lamp.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Lovely. Dinner and a specimen. And I don't suppose anyone's going to ask what she's done to them, because I'd bet the whole pot there's a list somewhere of what she's done to them.\"\n\n[[iyer]] \"They're tardigrades, Administrator, out of the soil cores, and I've been exposing them to the shielding dose in stages, which I would note is the only honest way to learn what a colony's crops might be bred to survive. The Chief of Security is welcome to his suspicion, provided he understands that the batch which lived is worth rather more than the batch which didn't.\"\n\nMichelle takes the jar back and screws the lid tight.", "choices": [{"label": "Laugh at Nolan's", "info": [["people", "Nolan"], ["danger", "Michelle's good opinion"]], "out": "Nolan grins and passes you the bread. Michelle puts the jar on her knee and eats the rest of the meal with perfect manners, and says nothing at all, and you suspect she is keeping count."}, {"label": "Take Michelle's side", "info": [["people", "Michelle"], ["danger", "Nolan, outnumbered"]], "out": "[[iyer]] \"I'm obliged, Administrator.\"\n\nMichelle sets the jar in the middle of the table where everyone can see it. Nolan says he'd like it on record that he asked, and then holds it up to the lamp for longer than anyone, looking for whatever it is she hasn't mentioned."}, {"label": "Ask Michelle what they're for", "note": "Michelle will tell you. At length, and priced.", "info": [["yield", "Something learned"], ["danger", "Nolan's supper"]], "out": "Michelle tells you, in long and courteous sentences, how much each dose cost her in specimens and what it bought, until the stew is cold. Nolan gets up halfway through to walk the cryo decks and leaves the plate. You come away knowing what a few thousand water bears are worth, to the nearest decimal."}]}, "zulu+iyer": {"title": "Something in a Jar", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nMichelle has brought a jar to supper and set it down beside the salt. Something no bigger than a grain of rice is swimming in it, thousands of them. Someone looks at it once and goes on eating.\n\nToby waits until she has finished serving herself.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Professor, I'd ask whether that has been cleared to sit near the food, because if it hasn't then I'd like it noted that I'm the one who has to answer for it.\"\n\n[[iyer]] \"They're tardigrades, Administrator, out of the soil cores, and I've been exposing them to the shielding dose in stages, which I would note is the only way to learn what a colony's crops might be bred to survive. The Chief of Security is quite right that I didn't ask, and I would also observe that I wouldn't have been given the answer I wanted.\"\n\nMichelle takes the jar back and screws the lid tight.", "choices": [{"label": "Back Toby", "info": [["people", "Toby"], ["danger", "Michelle's good opinion"]], "out": "You tell Michelle the jar goes back to the lab, and Toby thanks you and says he'll walk it down himself. Michelle hands it over with perfect manners and eats the rest of the meal without a word, and you suspect she is keeping count."}, {"label": "Back Michelle", "info": [["people", "Michelle"], ["danger", "Toby, outnumbered"]], "out": "[[iyer]] \"I'm obliged, Administrator.\"\n\nMichelle sets the jar in the middle of the table.\n\n[[zulu]] \"Understood.\" \"I'm sorry, Professor, I shouldn't have raised it at table.\"\n\nToby holds it up to the lamp for longer than anyone, looking for what she hasn't said."}, {"label": "Ask Michelle what they're for", "note": "Michelle will tell you. At length, and priced.", "info": [["yield", "Something learned"], ["danger", "Toby's supper"]], "out": "Michelle tells you, in long and courteous sentences, how much each dose cost her in specimens and what it bought, until the stew is cold. Toby listens politely to most of it, then excuses himself because it's the hour of his rounds, and the plate stays where it is. You come away knowing what a few thousand water bears are worth, to the nearest decimal."}]}},
  "soc.lights": {"dahl+kovacs": {"title": "Two on the Watch", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nNolan is counting the amber lights on the cryo board.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Forty-one amber, and there were thirty-nine at the last change, so who've we lost, Jeremy, and when exactly were you going to mention it?\"\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Nobody, it's the sensors, and I'll get to them.\"\n\nJeremy passes a flask.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"You count lights and I count bearings, so it's the same job really.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask what they'll miss about Earth", "ok": "Nolan had a dog, it turns out, a stupid one, and tells you every stupid thing it ever did. Jeremy has a daughter who'll be sixty by the time anyone wakes. They're still talking at ship's morning, and Jeremy leaves the flask with Nolan.", "bad": "Nolan says nobody back home will remember they ever existed, and that it's better that way. Jeremy gets up and goes to check a panel that doesn't need checking, and doesn't come back until morning."}, {"label": "Ask Jeremy straight how long the reactor has", "info": [["people", "Jeremy"], ["danger", "Nolan's sleep"]], "out": "Jeremy says it flat, like a weather report.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Forty-five years. Long enough, just, if I keep my hands on her.\"\n\nNolan laughs a little too long and asks for the flask back."}, {"label": "Leave them the flask and take the far console", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take the far console. When you look over they're arguing about something with real heat and enjoying it, and neither of them looks up."}]}, "zulu+kovacs": {"title": "Two on the Watch", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nToby is standing at the cryo board with his hands behind his back, reading the amber lights one at a time.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Jeremy, there are forty-one amber now and there were thirty-nine at the last change, and I'd ask you to tell me plainly whether any of the sleepers is in trouble, because I'd like to know before I tell myself it's nothing.\"\n\n[[kovacs]] \"It's the sensors, son, and nobody's in trouble, and I'll get to them.\"\n\nJeremy passes a flask.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"You watch the sleepers and I watch the bearings, so it's the same job really.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask what they'll miss about Earth", "ok": "Toby writes to his mother every rest day, to a house that will be gone before anyone answers, and he tells you so with great care, as if reporting it. Jeremy has a daughter who'll be sixty by the time anyone wakes. Neither of them sleeps, and Jeremy leaves the flask where Toby can reach it.", "bad": "Toby says he promised his mother he'd come home and he can't keep that now, and then he goes very quiet and very correct and asks to be excused. Jeremy gets up to check a panel that doesn't need checking, and doesn't come back until morning."}, {"label": "Ask Jeremy straight how long the reactor has", "info": [["people", "Jeremy"], ["danger", "Toby's sleep"]], "out": "Jeremy says it flat, like a weather report.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Forty-five years. Long enough, just, if I keep my hands on her.\"\n\nToby thanks him for the plain answer, and then stands a long while at the board counting the sleepers under his breath."}, {"label": "Leave them the flask and take the far console", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take the far console. When you look over, Toby is explaining the watch rota with great seriousness and Jeremy is telling him it's all wrong, and neither of them looks up."}]}, "dahl+halloran": {"title": "Two on the Watch", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nNolan is counting the amber lights on the cryo board.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Forty-one amber, and there were thirty-nine at the last change, so who've we lost, Roberta, and I'd love to know when you were planning on telling me, because I'm sure it was going to be soon.\"\n\n[[halloran]] \"Nobody, you suspicious bastard, it's a shit connector on the sensor bus, and I've written it up twice!\"\n\nRoberta bangs a mug of the stuff from the still down in front of him.\n\n[[halloran]] \"I'm going to rip the whole board out and do it right, so drink that and stop counting.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask what they'll miss about Earth", "ok": "Nolan had a dog, it turns out, a stupid one, and tells you every stupid thing it ever did. Roberta says she misses a pub, an actual pub, with a dartboard, and swears at it for a full minute with real love. They're still talking at ship's morning, and Roberta leaves the mug with Nolan.", "bad": "Nolan says nobody back home will remember they ever existed, and that it's better that way. Roberta goes quiet, which is worse than the swearing, and gets up to check a panel that doesn't need checking, and doesn't come back until morning."}, {"label": "Ask Roberta straight how long the reactor has", "info": [["people", "Roberta"], ["danger", "Nolan's sleep"]], "out": "[[halloran]] \"Forty-five years, boss! If somebody lets me put in proper bearings and stop nursing the old ones, and that's a big fucking if!\""}, {"label": "Leave them the mug and take the far console", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take the far console. When you look over they're shouting about something with real heat and enjoying it, and neither of them looks up."}]}, "zulu+halloran": {"title": "Two on the Watch", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nToby is standing at the cryo board with his hands behind his back, reading the amber lights one at a time.\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Roberta, there are forty-one amber now and there were thirty-nine at the last change, and I'd ask you to tell me plainly if any of the sleepers is in trouble, because they're mine to watch even while they sleep.\"\n\n[[halloran]] \"They're fine, Toby, nobody's in trouble, it's a shit connector on the sensor bus and I've written it up twice!\"\n\nRoberta bangs a mug of the stuff from the still down beside him.\n\n[[halloran]] \"I'm going to rip the whole board out and do it right, so drink that and sit down!\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask what they'll miss about Earth", "ok": "Toby writes to his mother every rest day, to a house that will be gone before anyone answers, and he tells you so with great care, as if reporting it. Roberta says she misses a pub with a dartboard and swears at it for a full minute with real love. They're still talking at ship's morning, and Roberta leaves the mug where Toby can reach it.", "bad": "Toby says he promised his mother he'd come home and he can't keep that now, and then he goes very quiet and very correct and asks to be excused. Roberta goes quiet too, which is worse than the swearing, and gets up to check a panel that doesn't need checking."}, {"label": "Ask Roberta straight how long the reactor has", "info": [["people", "Roberta"], ["danger", "Toby's sleep"]], "out": "[[halloran]] \"Forty-five years, boss! If somebody lets me put in proper bearings and stop nursing the old ones, and that's a big fucking if!\""}, {"label": "Leave them the mug and take the far console", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take the far console. When you look over, Toby is explaining the watch rota with great seriousness and Roberta is shouting that it's all wrong, and neither of them looks up."}]}},
  "soc.line": {"nakamura+solheim": {"title": "The Wardroom", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe waking crew eat in the mess two decks down. The officers eat up here, behind a hatch, and Andrea wants it stopped.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"They want to see us in the line with a tray, Jane.\" \"Eating what they're eating. That's all it is, and I don't know what it costs you to give them that.\"\n\n[[solheim]] \"We eat here and we talk shop, because nobody down there wants us looking at their tray.\"\n\nJane doesn't look up from the stores sheet.\n\n[[solheim]] \"Ten minutes. Then the reactor report.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Down to the mess with everyone", "info": [["people", "Andrea, and the crew"], ["danger", "Jane"]], "out": "The officers queue with a tray from the next night on. The crew are stiff about it for a week and then forget to be. Jane eats standing up and leaves first, every time."}, {"label": "The wardroom stays", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Andrea"]], "out": "The wardroom stays, and the suppers in it get more done than any meeting. Andrea eats in the sick bay with the night staff more often than not."}, {"label": "The mess once a week", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither is satisfied"]], "out": "Once a week, then, on rest day. Andrea calls it a start. Jane puts it on the roster like a drill, and the crew treat it like one."}]}, "brandt+solheim": {"title": "The Wardroom", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe waking crew eat in the mess two decks down. The officers eat up here, behind a hatch, and Lou has a reason for wanting that stopped.\n\nLou is stirring a pot he hasn't tasted.\n\n[[brandt]] \"You'll notice nobody has come up to the sick bay with a stomach complaint since we left.\" \"That isn't health, it's a hatch. I'd like to watch who clears their plate and who doesn't, and the only place to do it is the line.\"\n\n[[solheim]] \"We eat here and we talk shop.\"\n\nJane doesn't look up from the stores sheet.\n\n[[solheim]] \"If someone is off their food, the duty roster will show it before your line does. Ten minutes, then the reactor report.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Down to the mess with everyone", "info": [["people", "Lou, and the crew"], ["danger", "Jane"]], "out": "The officers queue with a tray from the next night on. Lou sits with his back to the wall and says nothing for a week, and in the second he has two crew in the sick bay with nothing worse than a bad tooth and a skipped meal. Jane eats standing up and leaves first, every time."}, {"label": "The wardroom stays", "info": [["people", "Jane"], ["danger", "Lou"]], "out": "The wardroom stays, and the suppers in it get more done than any meeting. Lou keeps a list of who he hasn't seen eat, and it is longer than he lets on."}, {"label": "The mess once a week", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither is satisfied"]], "out": "Once a week, then, on rest day. Lou calls it a sample too small to mean anything, and goes anyway. Jane puts it on the roster like a drill, and the crew treat it like one."}]}, "nakamura+achebe": {"title": "The Wardroom", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe waking crew eat in the mess two decks down. The officers eat up here, behind a hatch, and Andrea wants it stopped.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"They want to see us in the line with a tray, Lucas.\" \"Eating what they're eating. That's all it is, and I don't know why you of all people are making it hard.\"\n\n[[achebe]] \"Listen, Andrea, I hear you, and I mean it.\"\n\nLucas puts his spoon down.\n\n[[achebe]] \"But this hour is the one time every day all of us are in one room and talking straight, and I don't want to give that up for the sake of a tray. If we go down there, folks will watch their words, and so will we.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Down to the mess with everyone", "info": [["people", "Andrea, and the crew"], ["danger", "Lucas"]], "out": "The officers queue with a tray from the next night on. The crew are stiff about it for a week and then forget to be. Lucas says he's glad of it, and then he says it a second time, and you can tell he's thinking of the hour he lost."}, {"label": "The wardroom stays", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Andrea"]], "out": "The wardroom stays, and Lucas runs the hour like a meeting where nobody has to put a hand up. Andrea eats in the sick bay with the night staff more often than not, and he doesn't press her about it, which is worse."}, {"label": "The mess once a week", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither is satisfied"]], "out": "Once a week, then, on rest day. Andrea calls it a start. Lucas says that's fair, that's a fair deal, and asks the crew at the next line what they think of it."}]}, "brandt+achebe": {"title": "The Wardroom", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe waking crew eat in the mess two decks down. The officers eat up here, behind a hatch, and Lou has a reason for wanting that stopped.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Oh, good, we're all here.\" \"I'd like to put one question to you, Lucas. Two decks down there are a hundred-odd people sharing one serving line, and I'd quite like to be standing in it the day somebody's cough starts, rather than hearing about it from a rota.\"\n\n[[achebe]] \"I understand that, Lou, and it's a fair thing to ask.\"\n\nLucas puts his spoon down.\n\n[[achebe]] \"But this hour is the one time every day all of us are in one room and talking straight, and I'd hate to lose it. Folks down there can walk up here any evening, and I'd like them to.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Down to the mess with everyone", "info": [["people", "Lou, and the crew"], ["danger", "Lucas"]], "out": "The officers queue with a tray from the next night on. Lou watches the line like a man reading a chart, and finds a pair of fitters who haven't eaten properly in days and haven't liked to say. Lucas says he's glad of it, and you can tell he's thinking of the hour he lost."}, {"label": "The wardroom stays", "info": [["people", "Lucas"], ["danger", "Lou"]], "out": "The wardroom stays, and Lucas runs the hour like a meeting where nobody has to put a hand up. Lou goes down alone on his own time and says it's for the walk, and no one asks him again."}, {"label": "The mess once a week", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither is satisfied"]], "out": "Once a week, then, on rest day. Lou calls it a sample too small to mean anything, and goes anyway. Lucas says that's a fair deal, and asks the crew at the next line what they think of it."}]}},
  "soc.mould": {"yurbin+nakamura": {"title": "Under the Dressing", "text": "A fitter from the hull crew has a gash in the shin that won't close. Nothing heals well in the ship's dry air, and Andrea has cleaned it, cut it back, packed it and cleaned it again. The edges are going grey.\n\nMac has a fungus out of the soil cores that grows on dead things.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"It eats dead tissue, only dead, I've had it on a dish with live cells for a month and it'd rather starve than touch them, and it knows the difference better than we do, isn't that beautiful?\"\n\n[[nakamura]] \"You want to put something out of a soil core into an open leg.\" \"In my sick bay. On somebody who'd like to keep both of them.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Let Mac try it", "ok": "Mac lays it in with tweezers, talking the whole time. Five days later the wound is pink and clean to the edge. Andrea asks for a dish of it for the cabinet and doesn't say thank you, and Mac doesn't need it said.", "bad": "It takes, and it doesn't stop at the edge. By the third day it's in living muscle, and Andrea has the fitter on the table to take the leg below the knee. Andrea doesn't speak to Mac for the rest of the year."}, {"label": "Andrea's way: take the leg now, clean", "info": [["yield", "The fitter lives"], ["danger", "The fitter's leg"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "Andrea takes it below the knee that afternoon, clean, and the fitter is up on a crutch inside a month. Mac puts the dish in the incinerator and doesn't mention it again for a long time."}, {"label": "Have Mac prove it on Mac's own arm first", "info": [["yield", "The leg, if it works"], ["danger", "Mac's arm"]], "out": "Mac cuts a nick in one forearm that evening, lays the fungus in it and keeps notes. It eats the scab and stops. A month later the fitter's leg gets the same, and closes. Mac's arm has an ugly white scar that gets shown to anyone who sits still."}]}, "iyer+nakamura": {"title": "Under the Dressing", "text": "A fitter from the hull crew has a gash in the shin that won't close. Nothing heals well in the ship's dry air, and Andrea has cleaned it, cut it back, packed it and cleaned it again. The edges are going grey.\n\nMichelle has a fungus out of the soil cores that grows on dead things.\n\n[[iyer]] \"I would note, Administrator, that over a month of trials the organism consumed necrotic tissue and declined every living cell it was offered, which makes it, in my estimation, the most useful thing we've brought out of the cores, provided that someone is prepared to put it in a leg. I haven't asked the fitter, since I'd prefer to put it to him once the alternative has been explained.\"\n\n[[nakamura]] \"You want to put something out of a soil core into an open leg.\" \"In my sick bay, on a man who'd like to keep both of them, and who hasn't been asked, because that's not a conversation you get to have first.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Let Michelle try it", "ok": "Michelle lays it in on a schedule she's drawn up in advance and checks the edge at the same hour every day. Five days later the wound is pink and clean to the edge. Andrea asks for a dish of it for the cabinet and doesn't say thank you, and Michelle only writes it in the book as an outcome in the fitter's favour.", "bad": "It takes, and it doesn't stop at the edge. By the third day it's in living muscle, and Andrea has the fitter on the table to take the leg below the knee. Michelle goes to her lab and stays there two days, and what she says about it afterwards is that the dose was wrong. Andrea doesn't speak to her for the rest of the year."}, {"label": "Andrea's way: take the leg now, clean", "info": [["yield", "The fitter lives"], ["danger", "The fitter's leg"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "Andrea takes it below the knee that afternoon, clean, and the fitter is up on a crutch inside a month. Michelle puts the dish in the incinerator, enters it in the book as a result not obtained, and is a good deal more formal with you for a while."}, {"label": "Have Michelle prove it on her own arm first", "info": [["yield", "The leg, if it works"], ["danger", "Michelle's arm"]], "out": "Michelle cuts a nick in one forearm that evening without telling anyone, lays the fungus in it and logs it hourly in her even hand. It eats the scab and stops. A month later the fitter's leg gets the same, and closes. Her arm has a white scar, which she refers to, when she refers to it at all, as the control."}]}, "yurbin+brandt": {"title": "Under the Dressing", "text": "A fitter from the hull crew has a gash in the shin that won't close. Nothing heals well in the ship's dry air, and Lou has cleaned it, cut it back, packed it and cleaned it again. The edges are going grey.\n\nMac has a fungus out of the soil cores that grows on dead things.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"It eats dead tissue, only dead, I've had it on a dish with live cells for a month and it'd rather starve than touch them, and it knows the difference, which, how does it know the difference, no wait, that's the next dish, isn't that beautiful?\"\n\n[[brandt]] \"Oh, marvellous, a cure that grew in dirt.\" \"It stops at the dead part until the day it doesn't, and then I've a leg's worth of fungus with a blood supply, on a ship with nowhere to put the patients. You're not asking whether it works, you're asking whether I'll let you find out.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Let Mac try it", "ok": "Mac lays it in with tweezers, talking the whole time, while Lou stands by with the saline and says nothing. Five days later the wound is pink and clean to the edge. Lou asks for a dish of it for the cabinet, in case, and tells Mac not to make a habit of this, which Mac takes for a medal.", "bad": "It takes, and it doesn't stop at the edge. By the third day it's in living muscle, and Lou has the fitter on the table to take the leg below the knee. Lou tells Mac exactly what it cost, in order, once, and after that speaks to him only about work for the rest of the year."}, {"label": "Lou's way: take the leg now, clean", "info": [["yield", "The fitter lives"], ["danger", "The fitter's leg"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "Lou takes it below the knee that afternoon, clean, and the fitter is up on a crutch inside a month. Mac puts the dish in the incinerator and doesn't mention it again for a long time."}, {"label": "Have Mac prove it on Mac's own arm first", "info": [["yield", "The leg, if it works"], ["danger", "Mac's arm"]], "out": "Mac cuts a nick in one forearm that evening, lays the fungus in it and keeps notes. It eats the scab and stops. A month later the fitter's leg gets the same, and closes. Mac's arm has an ugly white scar that gets shown to anyone who sits still, and Lou sits through it with the air of a man being shown a rash."}]}, "iyer+brandt": {"title": "Under the Dressing", "text": "A fitter from the hull crew has a gash in the shin that won't close. Nothing heals well in the ship's dry air, and Lou has cleaned it, cut it back, packed it and cleaned it again. The edges are going grey.\n\nMichelle has a fungus out of the soil cores that grows on dead things.\n\n[[iyer]] \"I would note, Administrator, that over a month of trials the organism consumed necrotic tissue and declined every living cell it was offered, which makes it, in my estimation, the most useful thing we've brought out of the cores, provided that someone is prepared to put it in a leg.\"\n\n[[brandt]] \"Oh, how nice, a volunteer who hasn't been told he's one.\" \"If it gets past the dead part it's in the blood, and then I've a ship full of patients and a very interesting paper. You're not asking whether it works, Professor, you're asking whether you can run it before anyone with a licence says no.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Let Michelle try it", "ok": "Michelle lays it in on a schedule she's drawn up in advance, with Lou beside her counting the hours aloud in a voice with no hope in it. Five days later the wound is pink and clean to the edge. Lou asks for a dish of it for the cabinet and doesn't say thank you, and Michelle writes it in the book as an outcome in the fitter's favour.", "bad": "It takes, and it doesn't stop at the edge. By the third day it's in living muscle, and Lou has the fitter on the table to take the leg below the knee. Michelle goes to her lab and stays there two days, and what she says about it afterwards is that the dose was wrong. Lou says what he thinks of that once, evenly, and after it speaks to her only about work for the rest of the year."}, {"label": "Lou's way: take the leg now, clean", "info": [["yield", "The fitter lives"], ["danger", "The fitter's leg"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "Lou takes it below the knee that afternoon, clean, and the fitter is up on a crutch inside a month. Michelle puts the dish in the incinerator, enters it in the book as a result not obtained, and is a good deal more formal with you for a while."}, {"label": "Have Michelle prove it on her own arm first", "info": [["yield", "The leg, if it works"], ["danger", "Michelle's arm"]], "out": "Michelle cuts a nick in one forearm that evening without telling anyone, lays the fungus in it and logs it hourly in her even hand. It eats the scab and stops. A month later the fitter's leg gets the same, and closes. Her arm has a white scar, which she refers to, when she refers to it at all, as the control, and Lou checks it twice a week and calls that routine."}]}},
  "soc.names": {"yurbin+estrada": {"title": "Names on the Racks", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe hydroponics bay has its first crop up, forty racks of it, and every rack needs a label. Mac has been writing strain codes on them. Samuel has been crossing them out and writing the names of villages back home.\n\nMac says it over the stew.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"You can't call a wheat Santa Rosa.\" \"There are four Santa Rosas, Samuel, four, in three countries, and in a year nobody will know which wheat anyone means, a code only ever means the one thing, that's the whole beauty of it.\"\n\nSamuel taught Mac half of what Mac knows about growing things, and Mac has never once admitted it.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Folk'll remember Santa Rosa. Nobody's going to remember TR-114.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Mac's codes", "info": [["yield", "A proper catalogue"], ["danger", "Samuel"]], "out": "The racks get Mac's codes, in Mac's hand, with a line under each. The bay crews learn none of them and call every rack \"the tall one\" or \"the sad one\". The seed catalogue is the best-kept book on the ship."}, {"label": "Samuel's names", "info": [["people", "The bay crews"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "The racks get Samuel's names: Santa Rosa, Ixtlán, Little Hill, and one that's just \"Mother's\". Within a few meals the whole ship uses them. Mac keeps the codes in a notebook, and sulks."}, {"label": "Both, one above the other", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither gets the label"]], "out": "Both go on, the code above and the village below, and the labels have to be made twice the size. They argue over whose line goes on top for the rest of the year, and enjoy every minute of it."}]}, "iyer+estrada": {"title": "Names on the Racks", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe hydroponics bay has its first crop up, forty racks of it, and every rack needs a label. Michelle has had a code stencilled on each, to the trial standard. Samuel has been scraping the stencils off with a thumbnail and writing the names of villages back home.\n\n[[iyer]] \"I would remind you, Administrator, that there are four Santa Rosas in three countries, and that in a year's time no one will be able to say which wheat is meant by the name, whereas a code, provided it's entered correctly, can only ever mean the one thing.\"\n\nMichelle doesn't raise her voice, and she hasn't yet looked at the thumbnail.\n\nSamuel keeps scraping.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Folk'll remember Santa Rosa. Nobody's going to tend a thing they can't say.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Michelle's codes", "info": [["yield", "A proper catalogue"], ["danger", "Samuel"]], "out": "The racks keep Michelle's codes, stencilled square, with the line of descent beneath. Samuel puts the scraper down and says nothing to anyone. The bay crews call every rack \"the tall one\" or \"the pale one\", and the seed catalogue is the cleanest record on the ship."}, {"label": "Samuel's names", "info": [["people", "The bay crews"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "The racks get Samuel's names: Santa Rosa, Ixtlán, Little Hill, and one that's just \"Mother's\". Within a few meals the whole ship uses them. Michelle enters her codes in a ledger of her own and is never heard to say a single name aloud."}, {"label": "Both, one above the other", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither gets the label"]], "out": "Both go on, the code stencilled above and the village below in Samuel's hand, so the labels have to be made twice the size. Michelle calls it redundancy and Samuel calls it company, and they settle who answers for which line over a good many meals."}]}, "yurbin+waititi": {"title": "Names on the Racks", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe hydroponics bay has its first crop up, forty racks of it, and every rack needs a label. Mac has been writing strain codes on them. Hamond has been writing over the codes, in letters twice the size, with the names of relatives.\n\nMac says it over the stew.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"You can't call a wheat Aunt Berit's Revenge.\" \"Hamond, there are forty racks, forty, and in a year nobody will know which one's the revenge, a code only ever means the one thing, that's the whole beauty of it, and if you'd just, hold on, where's my notebook.\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"Ha! My friend, nobody ever got hungry for TR-114!\"\n\nHamond is ladling stew into everyone's bowl, Mac's twice.\n\n[[waititi]] \"The one by the hatch is Dalia's, and when she wakes up she'll read it for an hour and say it's too much, and I want her to have something to say it about.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Mac's codes", "info": [["yield", "A proper catalogue"], ["danger", "Hamond"]], "out": "The racks get Mac's codes, in Mac's hand, with a line under each. The bay crews learn none of them and call every rack \"the tall one\" or \"the sad one\". Hamond takes it loudly and well, and feeds the whole bay anyway, and the seed catalogue is the best-kept book on the ship."}, {"label": "Hamond's names", "info": [["people", "The bay crews"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "The racks get Hamond's names: Aunt Berit's, Uncle Tarek's, Dalia's by the hatch, and one that's only \"Mother's Mistake\". Within a few meals the whole ship uses them, and Hamond tells the story of each to anyone who stands still. Mac keeps the codes in a notebook, and sulks."}, {"label": "Both, one above the other", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither gets the label"]], "out": "Both go on, the code above and the name below, and the labels have to be made twice the size. They argue over whose line goes on top for the rest of the year, and Hamond promises Mac a loaf from every wheat that comes up, which he'll regret."}]}, "iyer+waititi": {"title": "Names on the Racks", "text": "{SUPPER}\n\nThe hydroponics bay has its first crop up, forty racks of it, and every rack needs a label. Michelle has had a code stencilled on each, to the trial standard. Hamond has been painting over the stencils, in letters twice the size, with the names of relatives.\n\n[[iyer]] \"I would point out, Administrator, that a rack called Aunt Berit's tells a future reader nothing about the cultivar, and that in a year's time a code will be the only label here that still means one thing.\"\n\nMichelle doesn't raise her voice, and she watches the brush the whole time.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Ha! My friend, nobody ever got hungry for a number!\"\n\nHamond doesn't stop painting.\n\n[[waititi]] \"The one by the hatch is Dalia's, and when she wakes up she'll read it for an hour and tell me it's too much, and I want her to have something to say it about.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Michelle's codes", "info": [["yield", "A proper catalogue"], ["danger", "Hamond"]], "out": "The racks keep Michelle's codes, stencilled square, with the line of descent beneath. Hamond puts the brush down and, for once, takes a full minute to say anything at all. The bay crews call every rack \"the tall one\" or \"the pale one\", and the seed catalogue is the cleanest record on the ship."}, {"label": "Hamond's names", "info": [["people", "The bay crews"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "The racks get Hamond's names: Aunt Berit's, Uncle Tarek's, Dalia's by the hatch, and one that's only \"Mother's Mistake\". Within a few meals the whole ship uses them. Michelle enters her codes in a ledger of her own and describes the names, to you alone, as an unreliable index."}, {"label": "Both, one above the other", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["danger", "Neither gets the label"]], "out": "Both go on, the code stencilled above and the name painted below, so the labels have to be made twice the size. Michelle calls it redundancy and Hamond calls it belt and braces, and they settle who answers for which line over a good many meals."}]}},
  "soc.racks": {"kovacs+estrada": {"title": "Water for the Racks", "text": "Samuel's crews water the hydroponic racks by hand, a can at a time, four hours a shift. Jeremy has a spare coolant pump and a coil of line, and reckons it'll mist the whole bay on a timer.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"She's a good pump. Wasted sitting in a crate. Give me two days and the parts and she'll water the lot.\"\n\nSamuel isn't sure.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Roots rot if they sit wet. Put that much on at once and you'll drown the bottom racks.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Jeremy's pump, every rack, full pressure", "ok": "The pump coughs, catches and hums. The bay is misted every hour on the hour, and the bay crews go back to pruning. Samuel stands at the end of a rack watching the drops come down, and says a word of thanks over it.", "bad": "It runs beautifully for a week. Then the bottom racks go soft and brown at the root, as Samuel said they would, and a month's growing goes in the composter. Jeremy shuts the pump off and doesn't argue."}, {"label": "The pump on Samuel's terms: a fine mist, top racks only", "info": [["yield", "Some of the work saved"], ["danger", "Jeremy's patience"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"]], "out": "Jeremy grumbles about running a good pump at a quarter of what it can do, and runs it that way. The crews water the bottom racks by hand and the top ones water themselves, and nothing rots."}, {"label": "Keep the cans", "info": [["yield", "The parts stay in the store"], ["danger", "Samuel's crews"], ["danger", "Jeremy"]], "out": "The pump goes back in its crate. The cans go on, four hours a shift, and the crews' hands crack in the dry air. Jeremy mentions the pump at supper, more than once."}]}, "halloran+estrada": {"title": "Water for the Racks", "text": "Samuel's crews water the hydroponic racks by hand, a can at a time, four hours a shift. Roberta has been down there twice already, swearing at the hoses the bay was plumbed with, and she has a spare coolant pump and a drum of proper line she wants to use to mist the whole bay on a timer.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Boss, those cans are a goddamn disgrace! I've got a pump sitting in a crate and a coil of real line, to gauge, and I can have every rack on a timer in two days. Two! Fuck the cans!\"\n\nSamuel isn't sure.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Roots rot if they sit wet. Put that much on at once and you'll drown the bottom racks. I'd sooner it came slow.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Roberta's pump, every rack, full pressure", "ok": "The pump catches first go and the whole bay is misted on the hour. Roberta stands at the end of a rack with a spanner in her fist, yelling at nobody in particular that it's perfect, and Samuel watches the drops come down and says a word of thanks over them. The bay crews go back to pruning.", "bad": "It runs beautifully for a week. Then the bottom racks go soft and brown at the root, exactly as Samuel said they would, and a month's growing goes in the composter. Roberta shuts the pump off and stands there a while.\n\n[[halloran]] \"That's on me, boss.\" \"I didn't listen to him.\""}, {"label": "The pump on Samuel's terms: a fine mist, top racks only", "info": [["yield", "Some of the work saved"], ["danger", "Roberta's patience"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"]], "out": "Roberta swears at the valve for most of an afternoon, throttling a pump that could flood the bay down to a sulk, and tells anyone who comes by that it's a crime. Then she fits the last nozzle with Samuel holding the light. The crews water the bottom racks by hand and the top ones water themselves, and nothing rots."}, {"label": "Keep the cans", "info": [["yield", "The parts stay in the store"], ["danger", "Samuel's crews"], ["danger", "Roberta"]], "out": "The pump goes back in its crate and Roberta slams the lid. The cans go on, four hours a shift, and the crews' hands crack in the dry air. Roberta brings it up at supper, loudly, more than once."}]}, "kovacs+waititi": {"title": "Water for the Racks", "text": "Hamond has told the bay crews they'll have lettuce by the new year, and they water the hydroponic racks by hand, a can at a time, four hours a shift. Jeremy has a spare coolant pump and a coil of line, and reckons it'll mist the whole bay on a timer.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"She's a good pump. Wasted sitting in a crate. Give me two days and the parts and she'll water the lot. What the roots make of it, I couldn't tell you, so don't go promising anyone anything.\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"My friend, it's the best idea since my mother's gravy!\" \"Every rack, every hour, let them drink! Ha! Dalia says I'd water myself if you handed me a hose.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Jeremy's pump, every rack, full pressure", "ok": "The pump coughs, catches and hums. The bay is misted every hour on the hour, and the bay crews go back to pruning. Hamond stands at the end of a rack with his arms out in the spray, telling the whole bay he's not crying, it's the water.", "bad": "It runs beautifully for a week. Then the bottom racks go soft and brown at the root, and a month's growing goes in the composter. Jeremy shuts the pump off and doesn't argue. Hamond goes down the rows apologising to each rack, loudly, so everyone can enjoy it."}, {"label": "Top racks on the pump, the bottom ones by can", "info": [["yield", "Some of the work saved"], ["danger", "Jeremy's patience"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"]], "out": "Jeremy grumbles about running a good pump at a quarter of what it can do, and runs it that way, with Hamond holding the torch and talking the entire time. Jeremy doesn't ask him to stop. The top racks water themselves, and Hamond takes a can in each fist and does the bottom ones with a string of crew behind him, and nothing rots."}, {"label": "Keep the cans", "info": [["yield", "The parts stay in the store"], ["danger", "The bay crews"], ["danger", "Jeremy"]], "out": "The pump goes back in its crate. The cans go on, four hours a shift, and Hamond makes a sing-song of it, but the crews' hands crack in the dry air all the same. Jeremy mentions the pump at supper, more than once."}]}, "halloran+waititi": {"title": "Water for the Racks", "text": "Hamond has told the bay crews they'll have lettuce by the new year, and they water the hydroponic racks by hand, a can at a time, four hours a shift. Roberta has a spare coolant pump and a drum of proper line, and she wants to mist the whole bay on a timer.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Boss! Boss, listen! I've got a pump, I've got real line, to gauge, and two days! Every rack on a timer, and no more lugging cans like it's some goddamn well!\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"My friend, I love her.\" \"I said lettuce, you know, I said it in front of everyone with my whole chest, and now here comes Roberta with a pump! Fill them up, I say, every rack, all the way! Ha!\"", "choices": [{"label": "Roberta's pump, every rack, full pressure", "ok": "The pump catches first go and the whole bay is misted on the hour. Roberta stands at the end of a rack yelling that it's perfect, and Hamond stands beside her with his arms out in the spray, telling the whole bay he's not crying, it's the water. The crews go back to pruning.", "bad": "It runs beautifully for a week. Then the bottom racks go soft and brown at the root, and a month's growing goes in the composter. Roberta shuts the pump off and stands there a while.\n\n[[halloran]] \"That's on me, boss.\"\n\nHamond goes down the rows apologising to each rack, loudly, so everyone can enjoy it."}, {"label": "Top racks on the pump, the bottom ones by can", "info": [["yield", "Some of the work saved"], ["danger", "Roberta's patience"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"]], "out": "Roberta swears at the valve for most of an afternoon, throttling a pump that could flood the bay, while Hamond holds the light and tells her about his uncle Tarek's well. She fits the last nozzle with a few choice words. The top racks water themselves, and Hamond takes a can in each fist and does the bottom ones with a string of crew behind him, and nothing rots."}, {"label": "Keep the cans", "info": [["yield", "The parts stay in the store"], ["danger", "The bay crews"], ["danger", "Roberta"]], "out": "The pump goes back in its crate and Roberta slams the lid. The cans go on, four hours a shift, and Hamond makes a sing-song of it, but the crews' hands crack in the dry air all the same. Roberta brings it up at supper, loudly, more than once."}]}},
  "soc.sap": {"yurbin+kovacs": {"title": "Resin in the Seals", "text": "The reactor's coolant seals are perishing faster than the manual says they should, and every new one Jeremy fits comes out of the spares that have to last forty years. Mac has been growing a resin off a fungus culture that sets like rubber in an hour.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"It holds heat, it holds pressure, I've had it boiling for a week, Jeremy, a week, and it doesn't care, it just sits there being rubber, do you know how rare that is in something that grew itself?\"\n\nJeremy turns a lump of it over in one big greasy hand.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"You want to put mushroom glue in my reactor. In her. In the old girl.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Mac's resin", "ok": "Jeremy fits it in one seal, then in all of them, swearing the whole time. A month on they're tighter than the factory ones.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Don't tell Mac I said so.\"\n\nJeremy goes and tells Mac.", "bad": "It holds for nine days. On the tenth the heat turns it to glass and it cracks, and the reactor dumps coolant on the deck before Jeremy can trip it. Jeremy comes to supper with the cracked seal and puts it on Mac's plate."}, {"label": "Jeremy's way: new seals from the spares", "info": [["yield", "Seals that will hold"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "Jeremy fits factory seals, one an evening, and they're fine. Mac leaves the lump of resin on the workbench, where it sits for years as a paperweight."}, {"label": "Try it on the cold loop first, where a leak won't matter", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["yield", "A spare part, maybe"]], "out": "Jeremy puts one seal of resin on the cold loop and checks it every morning. By the end of the month it has held, and Jeremy goes on to the rest without being asked. Mac acts as if it was never in doubt."}]}, "iyer+kovacs": {"title": "Resin in the Seals", "text": "The reactor's coolant seals are perishing faster than the manual says they should, and every new one Jeremy fits comes out of the spares that have to last forty years. Michelle has bred a resin from a culture in her lab, and it sets like rubber in an hour.\n\n[[iyer]] \"It has held at temperature and pressure for eleven days, Administrator, which is a longer record than the last three seals Mr Donadini fitted, and I would note that the only argument I've heard against it is that it came out of a dish and not a crate.\"\n\nJeremy turns a lump of it over in one big greasy hand.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Eleven days. And there's already one in the auxiliary pump, did you know that? Nobody asked me. Now you want mushroom glue in the reactor, in the old girl, on the strength of what happened in a dish.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Michelle's resin", "ok": "Jeremy fits it in one seal, then in all of them, swearing the whole time. A month on they're tighter than the factory ones.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Don't tell her I said so.\"\n\nJeremy goes and tells her. Michelle says only that it agrees with her figures to within a percent, Administrator, which she'd expected, and that she'll want the remaining seals refitted the same way.", "bad": "It holds for nine days. On the tenth the heat turns it to glass and it cracks, and the reactor dumps coolant on the deck before Jeremy can trip it. Jeremy carries the cracked seal up to the lab and sets it on Michelle's bench, and she turns it under the lamp for a long while before she says the failure came at a temperature her runs never reached, Administrator, and that she'll be revising the numbers."}, {"label": "Jeremy's way: new seals from the spares", "info": [["yield", "Seals that will hold"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "Jeremy fits factory seals, one an evening, and they're fine. Michelle takes her resin back to the lab without a word, and Jeremy hears later that she's gone on running it on her own bench, to learn how long it takes to fail."}, {"label": "Try it on the cold loop first, where a leak won't matter", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["yield", "A spare part, maybe"]], "out": "Jeremy puts one seal of resin on the cold loop and checks it every morning. By the end of the month it has held, and Jeremy goes on to the rest without being asked. Michelle says the figures never gave her cause to doubt it, Administrator, and asks which loop is next."}]}, "yurbin+halloran": {"title": "Resin in the Seals", "text": "The reactor's coolant seals are perishing faster than the manual says they should, and every new one Roberta fits comes out of the spares that have to last forty years. Mac has been growing a resin off a fungus culture that sets like rubber in an hour.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"It holds heat, it holds pressure, I've had it boiling for a week, Roberta, a week, and it doesn't care, it just sits there being rubber, do you know how rare that is in something that, no wait, you're going to say it's a bodge, but it isn't, it's a, hold on.\"\n\n[[halloran]] \"It's a fucking mushroom, Mac!\"\n\nRoberta snatches the lump and squeezes it.\n\n[[halloran]] \"You want to put this in the reactor, boss? This bastard needs proper seals, to gauge, and I'll cut them out of the plate stock myself if I have to!\"", "choices": [{"label": "Mac's resin", "ok": "Roberta fits it in one seal, then in all of them, shouting at it the whole time. A month on they're tighter than the factory ones.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Don't you tell Mac I said so, boss!\"\n\nRoberta goes and tells Mac.", "bad": "It holds for nine days. On the tenth the heat turns it to glass and it cracks, and the reactor dumps coolant on the deck before Roberta can trip it.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Goddamn mushroom!\"\n\nRoberta comes to supper with the cracked seal and slaps it down on Mac's plate."}, {"label": "Roberta's way: proper seals from the spares", "info": [["yield", "Seals that will hold"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"], ["danger", "Mac"]], "out": "Roberta machines factory-gauge seals, one an evening, shouting at the lathe the whole time, and they're fine. Mac leaves the lump of resin on the workbench, where it sits for years as a paperweight."}, {"label": "Try it on the cold loop first, where a leak won't matter", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["yield", "A spare part, maybe"]], "out": "Roberta puts one seal of resin on the cold loop and checks it every morning, swearing at it. By the end of the month it has held, and she goes on to the rest without being asked. Mac acts as if it was never in doubt."}]}, "iyer+halloran": {"title": "Resin in the Seals", "text": "The reactor's coolant seals are perishing faster than the manual says they should, and every new one Roberta fits comes out of the spares that have to last forty years. Michelle has bred a resin from a culture in her lab, and it sets like rubber in an hour.\n\n[[iyer]] \"It has held at temperature and pressure for eleven days, Administrator, which is a longer record than the last three seals Craigie fitted, and I would note that the only argument I've heard against it is that it came out of a dish and not a crate.\"\n\n[[halloran]] \"Eleven days! Eleven!\"\n\nRoberta holds a lump of it up to the light.\n\n[[halloran]] \"And she's already put one in the auxiliary pump and told nobody, boss! This is a goddamn science project, and I'm the one who has to crawl in after it when it goes! This bastard needs proper seals, to gauge, and I'll make them myself!\"", "choices": [{"label": "Michelle's resin", "ok": "Roberta fits it in one seal, then in all of them, shouting at it the whole time. A month on they're tighter than the factory ones.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Don't you tell her I said so, boss!\"\n\nRoberta goes and tells her. Michelle says only that it agrees with her figures to within a percent, Administrator, which she'd expected, and that she'll want the remaining seals refitted the same way.", "bad": "It holds for nine days. On the tenth the heat turns it to glass and it cracks, and the reactor dumps coolant on the deck before Roberta can trip it.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Fuck!\"\n\nRoberta carries the cracked seal up to the lab and bangs it down on Michelle's bench, and Michelle turns it under the lamp for a long while before she says the failure came at a temperature her runs never reached, Administrator, and that she'll be revising the numbers."}, {"label": "Roberta's way: proper seals from the spares", "info": [["yield", "Seals that will hold"], ["danger", "Two spare parts"], ["danger", "Michelle"]], "out": "Roberta machines factory-gauge seals, one an evening, shouting at the lathe the whole time, and they're fine. Michelle takes her resin back to the lab without a word, and Roberta hears later that she's gone on running it on her own bench, to learn how long it takes to fail."}, {"label": "Try it on the cold loop first, where a leak won't matter", "info": [["people", "Both of them, a little"], ["yield", "A spare part, maybe"]], "out": "Roberta puts one seal of resin on the cold loop and checks it every morning, swearing at it. By the end of the month it has held, and she goes on to the rest without being asked. Michelle says the figures never gave her cause to doubt it, Administrator, and asks which loop is next."}]}},
  "soc.scar": {"dahl+nakamura": {"title": "Stitches", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nAndrea put Nolan back together once, on the launch docks, and Nolan has never said thank you. The scar through the eyebrow is from that night. Neither of them has mentioned it in four hours.\n\nNolan is cleaning a sidearm that's already clean. Andrea watches.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"You'll wear the barrel through, Nolan. Put it down and eat something.\"\n\n[[dahl]] \"Then I'll have a job tomorrow.\"\n\nNolan doesn't look up.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Lovely night for it.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Nolan about the scar", "info": [["people", "Nolan and Andrea"], ["danger", "Nolan's temper"]], "ok": "Nolan tells it badly, then Andrea tells it properly: a riot on the cargo dock, a pipe wrench, nine stitches and Nolan complaining through every one. By the end they're both laughing. At ship's morning Nolan says it to nobody in particular.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Thanks, doc.\"", "bad": "Nolan says it's none of your business, then says something worse about Andrea's sick bay that isn't true. Andrea leaves the flight deck. Nolan finishes the sidearm and starts it again."}, {"label": "Stand the rest of Nolan's watch yourself", "info": [["people", "Nolan, a night's sleep"], ["danger", "Your own night's sleep"]], "out": "Nolan hands you the log and goes to bed without arguing, which says enough. Andrea tells you Nolan hasn't slept a whole night since the burn. You hadn't known."}, {"label": "Leave them be", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug and go. Not much is said on the flight deck that night, but Andrea is up there again the next night with two mugs."}]}, "zulu+nakamura": {"title": "Stitches", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nAndrea closed Toby's left palm once, on the launch docks, after he caught a falling cargo strap bare-handed to keep it off a trainee. He wrote her a full page of thanks the next morning, and she has never mentioned it. The white line across his hand is from that night. Neither of them has said a word about it in four hours.\n\nToby comes back from the outer lock and enters the seals in the log. Andrea counts on her fingers.\n\n[[nakamura]] \"That's three times tonight, Toby. Sit down and eat something.\"\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Andrea, the seals were sound the first time and the second.\"\n\nToby stays standing.\n\n[[zulu]] \"I'd like to know they're still sound on the third, and then I'll eat.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Toby about his hand", "info": [["people", "Toby and Andrea"], ["danger", "Toby's pride"]], "ok": "Toby tells it in order, the strap first and the trainee second, and Andrea stops him to say it was four stitches and he apologised through every one. He starts to correct her and then stops, and then, for once, he's laughing. At ship's morning he thanks her again at the hatch, properly, and she lets him.", "bad": "Toby goes very quiet and very correct. He says the sick bay was entirely in order and that he should never have needed it, and Andrea hears a reproach in that and leaves the flight deck. Toby goes back out to walk the seals a fourth time."}, {"label": "Stand the rest of Toby's watch yourself", "info": [["people", "Toby, a night's sleep"], ["danger", "Your own night's sleep"]], "out": "Toby hands you the log and asks that it be noted he left his post by order, and then he goes to bed without another word. Andrea tells you Toby hasn't slept a whole night since the burn, because he walks the ship in his head. You hadn't known."}, {"label": "Leave them be", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug and go. Not much is said on the flight deck that night, but Andrea is up there again the next night with two mugs, and Toby sits down to drink his."}]}, "dahl+brandt": {"title": "Stitches", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nLou put Nolan back together once, on the launch docks, and Nolan has never said thank you. The scar through the eyebrow is from that night. Neither of them has mentioned it in four hours.\n\nNolan is cleaning a sidearm that's already clean. Lou watches him do it.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Oh, marvellous, the fourth time tonight. I don't believe you're worried about the barrel, you know, I think you're worried about whatever you imagine it's for, and I'd eat something before you find out.\"\n\n[[dahl]] \"And if I eat, I'm busy chewing when somebody's in the stores, and then it's my fault, isn't it.\"\n\nNolan doesn't look up.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Lovely night for it.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Nolan about the scar", "info": [["people", "Nolan and Lou"], ["danger", "Nolan's temper"]], "ok": "Nolan tells it badly, then Lou tells it properly: a brawl on the cargo dock, a pipe wrench, nine stitches and Nolan complaining through every one, until Lou threatened to bill him for the thread. By the end Nolan is laughing. At ship's morning Nolan says it to nobody in particular.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Thanks, doc.\"\n\nLou says he didn't hear anything.", "bad": "Nolan says it's none of your business, then says something worse about Lou's sick bay that isn't true. Lou answers in the same voice he'd use for a pulse.\n\n[[brandt]] \"Noted.\"\n\nHe leaves the flight deck. Nolan finishes the sidearm and starts it again."}, {"label": "Stand the rest of Nolan's watch yourself", "info": [["people", "Nolan, a night's sleep"], ["danger", "Your own night's sleep"]], "out": "Nolan hands you the log and goes to bed without arguing, which says enough. Lou tells you Nolan hasn't slept a whole night since the burn, and that he'd be obliged if you didn't say where you heard it. You hadn't known."}, {"label": "Leave them be", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug and go. Not much is said on the flight deck that night, but Lou is up there again the next night with two mugs, saying he happened to be passing."}]}, "zulu+brandt": {"title": "Stitches", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nLou closed Toby's left palm once, on the launch docks, after he caught a falling cargo strap bare-handed to keep it off a trainee. Toby thanked him so many times that Lou finally told him to stop. The white line across his hand is from that night. Neither of them has said a word about it in four hours.\n\nToby comes back from the outer lock and enters the seals in the log. Lou doesn't look up from his tablet.\n\n[[brandt]] \"That's three times tonight, and I'll point out the lock hasn't changed its mind. Eat something, and then tell me what you're expecting to come through it.\"\n\n[[zulu]] \"With respect, Doctor, I'm not expecting anything.\"\n\nToby stays standing.\n\n[[zulu]] \"I'd like to keep it that way, so I look.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Toby about his hand", "info": [["people", "Toby and Lou"], ["danger", "Toby's pride"]], "ok": "Toby tells it in order, the strap first and the trainee second, and Lou corrects the number of stitches and the number of apologies, both upwards. Toby starts to object and then, for once, he's laughing. At ship's morning he thanks Lou at the hatch, properly, and Lou says not to make a habit of it.", "bad": "Toby goes very quiet and very correct and says he'd ask that it not be discussed. Lou tells him, mildly, that he isn't embarrassed about the hand, he's embarrassed that it needed anyone.\n\n[[zulu]] \"Understood.\"\n\nToby goes out to walk the seals a fourth time, and Lou stays where he is."}, {"label": "Stand the rest of Toby's watch yourself", "info": [["people", "Toby, a night's sleep"], ["danger", "Your own night's sleep"]], "out": "Toby hands you the log and asks that it be noted he left his post by order, and then he goes to bed without another word. Lou tells you Toby hasn't slept a whole night since the burn, and that it's a poor sign in a man of twenty-nine. You hadn't known."}, {"label": "Leave them be", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug and go. Not much is said on the flight deck that night, but Lou is up there again the next night with two mugs, saying he happened to be passing, and Toby sits down to drink his."}]}},
  "soc.sky": {"yurbin+estrada": {"title": "The Big Window", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMac hasn't looked at the board once: the star chart in one hand, a pencil in the other, nose to the big window. Samuel is saying the night prayer, quietly, to the same stars.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"There's a smudge there that isn't on the chart.\" \"Not in the catalogue, not on last year's plate, nothing, it's just there, and I've been looking at it for an hour and I don't want to stop, isn't that wonderful?\"\n\nSamuel finishes the prayer before answering.\n\n[[estrada]] \"It's on somebody's chart. Just not yours.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Mac to show you", "ok": "Mac shows you a faint smear of light that moves against the stars, slowly, and says it's a comet nobody on Earth has seen yet. Samuel asks what to call it. They argue about it until morning and settle on something neither of them will tell you.", "bad": "Mac gets going on how far the light has come and how long its star has been dead, and somewhere in it says there's nobody out here to hear a prayer. Samuel stops talking. Mac doesn't notice for an hour, and then can't take it back."}, {"label": "Ask Samuel to say one for the watch", "info": [["people", "Samuel"], ["danger", "Mac, kept waiting"]], "out": "Samuel says it again, louder, for the three of you and for the sleepers. Mac stands with the chart folded, listening, and says amen in the wrong place."}, {"label": "Leave them to the window", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug to the far console. When you look back they're sitting on the step under the window side by side, and Mac is holding the chart so Samuel can see it."}]}, "iyer+estrada": {"title": "The Big Window", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMichelle hasn't looked at the board once. She stands at the big window with the plate reader and a stylus, taking a reading off one patch of sky and writing it down, then taking another. Samuel is saying the night prayer, quietly, to the same stars.\n\n[[iyer]] \"There is an object there that appears neither in the catalogue nor on last year's plate, Administrator, and I've now measured it eleven times, in which case I'd suggest that it's real, and that it moves, and that I would be obliged if you didn't mention it at muster until I've decided what to call it.\"\n\nSamuel finishes the prayer before answering.\n\n[[estrada]] \"It's on somebody's chart, Michelle. Just not ours.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Michelle to show you", "ok": "Michelle puts the plate reader in your hands and shows you a faint smear of light that moves against the stars, slowly, and gives you its distance and its period to three figures. It's a comet nobody on Earth has logged. Samuel asks what it's to be called, and they argue about it until morning and settle on something neither of them will tell you.", "bad": "Michelle explains, evenly, that the light left its star before any prayer was made, and that nothing it passed on the way was in a position to answer one, which she regards as a useful fact. Samuel stops talking. Michelle goes back to her readings, and when she does look up she doesn't take it back."}, {"label": "Ask Samuel to say one for the watch", "info": [["people", "Samuel"], ["danger", "Michelle, kept waiting"]], "out": "Samuel says it again, louder, for the three of you and for the sleepers. Michelle stands with the plate reader lowered and her eyes on the glass, and when he's done she writes the time in the log."}, {"label": "Leave them to the window", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug to the far console. When you look back they're sitting on the step under the window side by side, and Michelle is holding the plate reader so Samuel can see the figures."}]}, "yurbin+waititi": {"title": "The Big Window", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMac hasn't looked at the board once: the star chart in one hand, a pencil in the other, nose to the big window. Hamond has come up behind him with a covered pot and a ladle, and is explaining the sky to it as if it were a table of guests.\n\n[[yurbin]] \"There's a smudge there that isn't on the chart.\" \"Not in the catalogue, not on last year's plate, nothing, it's just there, and I've been looking at it for an hour and I don't want to stop, isn't that wonderful?\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"A smudge! Ha! I had a smudge on my good shirt once and my mother said it was a map of somewhere I'd never get to.\"\n\nHamond lifts the lid and the whole flight deck smells of leeks.\n\n[[waititi]] \"So go on, my friend, show me where it is, and then somebody eat something.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Mac to show you", "ok": "Mac shows you a faint smear of light that moves against the stars, slowly, and says it's a comet nobody on Earth has seen yet. Hamond wants to know what to call it. They argue about it until morning and settle on something neither of them will tell you, though Hamond announces twice that he isn't telling.", "bad": "Mac gets going on how far the light has come and how long its star has been dead, and somewhere in it says everything out there is already gone and nobody is waiting at the other end. Hamond stops laughing, and says it plainly.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Dalia is.\"\n\nHe puts the lid back on the pot. Mac doesn't notice for an hour, and then can't take it back."}, {"label": "Ask Hamond to put the pot on for the watch", "info": [["people", "Hamond"], ["danger", "Mac, kept waiting"]], "out": "Hamond ladles it into three mugs with a long speech about leeks, and says Dalia can't stand them and would eat the lot anyway. Mac stands at the window with the chart folded, eating without tasting a thing, and says it's wonderful."}, {"label": "Leave them to the window", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug to the far console. When you look back they're sitting on the step under the window side by side, Mac holding the chart so Hamond can see it and Hamond passing the pot."}]}, "iyer+waititi": {"title": "The Big Window", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nMichelle hasn't looked at the board once. She stands at the big window with the plate reader and a stylus, taking a reading off one patch of sky and writing it down, then taking another. Hamond has come up behind her with a covered pot and a ladle, and is telling the stars it's well past supper.\n\n[[iyer]] \"There is an object there that appears neither in the catalogue nor on last year's plate, Administrator, and I've now measured it eleven times, in which case I'd suggest that it's real, and that it moves, and that I would be obliged if you didn't mention it at muster until I've decided what to call it.\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"Eleven times, Professor! Ha! I'd be on my twelfth bowl by now.\"\n\nHamond lifts the lid and the whole flight deck smells of leeks.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Show me, my friend, and then somebody eat something.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Ask Michelle to show you", "ok": "Michelle puts the plate reader in your hands and shows you a faint smear of light that moves against the stars, slowly, and gives you its distance and its period to three figures. It's a comet nobody on Earth has logged. Hamond wants to know what it's to be called, and they argue about it until morning and settle on something neither of them will tell you, though Hamond announces twice that he isn't telling.", "bad": "Michelle remarks, evenly, that nobody in the cold banks will ever know this was seen, which she regards as an economy. Hamond puts the ladle down, and says it plainly.\n\n[[waititi]] \"That's my wife you're talking about.\"\n\nHe puts the lid back on the pot. Michelle returns to her readings and doesn't take it back."}, {"label": "Ask Hamond to put the pot on for the watch", "info": [["people", "Hamond"], ["danger", "Michelle, kept waiting"]], "out": "Hamond ladles it into three mugs with a long speech about leeks, and says Dalia can't stand them and would eat the lot anyway. Michelle takes hers without looking away from the glass, and an hour later you notice the mug is empty and she has written down what she thought of it."}, {"label": "Leave them to the window", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You take your mug to the far console. When you look back they're sitting on the step under the window side by side, Michelle holding the plate reader so Hamond can see the figures and Hamond passing the pot."}]}},
  "soc.stones": {"kovacs+estrada": {"title": "The Quiet Shift", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nTwo of the quietest people on the ship on one watch. They've been up here four hours and, by the log, said eleven words between them. They've scratched a board into a spare console panel and are playing a game with washers that nobody else understands.\n\nJeremy moves a washer. Samuel looks at it for a long time, then moves another.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Hm.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Sit in and play the winner", "ok": "You lose, twice, which is right. Jeremy explains the rules after the second game, which takes one sentence. Samuel laughs at something you do with a washer, and you realise you've never heard Samuel laugh.", "bad": "Somehow you win the first game. Jeremy looks at the board for a long time and goes back to the console. Samuel puts the washers away. Nobody mentions a rematch."}, {"label": "Ask what the colony will look like in twenty years", "ok": "Samuel sees orchards, and a field you can't see the end of. Jeremy sees a proper workshop with a roof that doesn't leak and a lathe that isn't held together with wire. It takes them an hour to say it, between moves, and you go to bed believing it.", "bad": "[[kovacs]] \"Twenty years?\"\n\nJeremy moves a washer.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"The old girl won't last the trip, so I'd not be asking her for twenty years on top of it.\"\n\nSamuel says nothing, which is worse, and the game goes on in a different kind of quiet."}, {"label": "Leave them the game", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You leave them to it. In the morning the panel has a second game scratched beside the first, and a third, half done."}]}, "halloran+estrada": {"title": "Washers", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nSamuel has been up here four hours and has said about eleven words. Roberta has said the rest, all of them to a game of washers scratched into a spare console panel, which she is losing.\n\n[[halloran]] \"No. No, no, no! Where did that one come from, I didn't see that, that's a goddamn ambush!\"\n\nSamuel looks at the board for a long time, as though it were weather, and moves one washer.\n\n[[estrada]] \"Hm.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Sit in and play the winner", "ok": "You lose, twice, which is right. Roberta explains the rules after the second game at the top of her voice and gets two of them wrong, and Samuel puts her right without raising his. Then Samuel laughs at something you do with a washer, and you realise you've never heard him laugh.", "bad": "Somehow you win the first game.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Well, shit, boss!\"\n\nRoberta goes back to the console to bang on something that wasn't broken. Samuel puts the washers away. Nobody mentions a rematch."}, {"label": "Ask what the colony will look like in twenty years", "ok": "Samuel sees orchards, and a field you can't see the end of. Roberta sees a workshop with a real lathe, bolted down and trued to gauge, and not one thing in it held up with wire. It takes them an hour to say it, between moves, and you go to bed believing it.", "bad": "[[halloran]] \"Twenty years?\"\n\nRoberta slaps down a washer.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Boss, this bastard of a ship won't make the trip without somebody properly rebuilding her, and I'm only one person!\"\n\nSamuel says nothing, which is worse, and the game goes on in a different kind of quiet."}, {"label": "Leave them the game", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You leave them to it. In the morning the panel has a second game scratched beside the first, and a third, half done, with a rule written next to it in Roberta's capitals and crossed out in somebody's pencil."}]}, "kovacs+waititi": {"title": "The Quiet Shift", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nOne of the quietest people on the ship and one of the loudest, on one watch. By the log, Jeremy has said eleven words in four hours and Hamond has said the rest. Between them on a spare console panel is a board scratched in with a nail, and they're playing a game with washers that nobody else understands.\n\nJeremy moves a washer.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Now that one is how my uncle Tarek used to move, my friend, slowly and with a face like a closed door, and he never won a game in his life, ha!\"\n\n[[kovacs]] \"Hm.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Sit in and play the winner", "ok": "You lose, twice, which is right. Jeremy explains the rules after the second game, which takes one sentence, and Hamond tells the story of how he learned them, which takes a good deal longer. Jeremy laughs at something you do with a washer, a short rough sound, and you realise you've never heard him laugh.", "bad": "Somehow you win the first game. Jeremy looks at the board for a long time and goes back to the console. Hamond puts the washers away, talking cheerfully the whole time, and nobody mentions a rematch."}, {"label": "Ask what the colony will look like in twenty years", "ok": "Hamond sees bread and orchards, and a long table with Dalia at the end of it telling him he's talking too much. Jeremy sees a proper workshop with a roof that doesn't leak and a lathe that isn't held together with wire. It takes them an hour to say it, between moves, and you go to bed believing it.", "bad": "[[kovacs]] \"Twenty years?\"\n\nJeremy moves a washer.\n\n[[kovacs]] \"The old girl won't last the trip, and I'm not going to promise anybody a bakery on the back of her.\"\n\nHamond opens his mouth and shuts it again, which you have never seen, and the game goes on in a different kind of quiet."}, {"label": "Leave them the game", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You leave them to it. In the morning the panel has a second game scratched beside the first, and a third, half done. Hamond is telling someone about it at breakfast and Jeremy is pretending not to listen."}]}, "halloran+waititi": {"title": "The Loud Shift", "text": "{WATCH}\n\nTwo of the loudest people on the ship on one watch, and you heard them from the corridor. They've scratched a board into a spare console panel and are playing a game with washers, and so far as you can tell each of them is playing by rules the other one made up.\n\n[[halloran]] \"That's a capture, you bastard!\"\n\n[[waititi]] \"It is not a capture, my friend.\" \"It's a very friendly move, and I'm sorry you're taking it so personally, ha!\"", "choices": [{"label": "Sit in and play the winner", "ok": "You lose, twice, which is right. They both explain the rules after the second game at once, which takes ten minutes and agrees on nothing. Then Roberta laughs at something you do with a washer, a great bark of a laugh, and Hamond laughs because she did, and you stay till the watch changes.", "bad": "Somehow you win the first game.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Well, shit, boss!\"\n\nRoberta goes back to the console to bang on something that wasn't broken. Hamond puts the washers away, still talking, and nobody mentions a rematch."}, {"label": "Ask what the colony will look like in twenty years", "ok": "Hamond sees bread and orchards, and a long table with Dalia at the end of it. Roberta sees a workshop with a real lathe, bolted down and trued to gauge, and not one thing in it held up with wire. It takes them an hour to say it, both at once and between moves, and you go to bed believing it.", "bad": "[[halloran]] \"Twenty years?\"\n\nRoberta slaps down a washer.\n\n[[halloran]] \"Boss, this bastard of a ship won't make the trip without somebody properly rebuilding her, and now you want me to plan a lathe?\"\n\nHamond opens his mouth and shuts it again, which you have never seen, and the game goes on in a different kind of quiet."}, {"label": "Leave them the game", "info": [["people", "The two of them"], ["danger", "Nothing in it for you"]], "out": "You leave them to it. In the morning the panel has a second game scratched beside the first, and a third, half done, with rules for each of them written alongside in two different hands. Both rule sets are crossed out."}]}},
  "soc.stores": {"dahl+estrada": {"title": "Short in the Stores", "text": "Things are walking out of the stores Samuel keeps: a sack of seed one week, a coil of cable the next. Samuel has started sleeping in there, which isn't helping anything.\n\nNolan has an idea, and is enjoying it.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Leave a sack of the good stuff out and dust the inside with dye, and whoever it is glows green for a week, and then we have a chat, and I'll be very civil about it.\"\n\n[[estrada]] \"Or.\" \"we ask at supper. Whoever it is, they're hungry or they're frightened. Either way they'll come and say.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Nolan's trap", "ok": "It takes four days. A young technician comes on shift with green hands and a story about a rail, and the seed is under a bunk, traded for cigarettes nobody should still have. Nolan has the chat. Samuel sits in on it, and the technician ends up on Samuel's crew instead of in the brig.", "bad": "Half the bay crew handle the sack on the first morning, on honest business, and come up green to the elbow. The real thief never touches it. Samuel's crews don't speak to Nolan's detail for a month."}, {"label": "Samuel's way: ask at supper", "info": [["people", "Samuel"], ["danger", "Nolan's fun"], ["danger", "A week of waiting"]], "out": "Nobody comes forward for a week. Then a young technician does, in tears, and the seed comes back. Nolan calls it the least interesting solution in the history of the species."}, {"label": "Let it go. It's seed", "info": [["danger", "The stores"], ["danger", "Both of them"]], "out": "Nothing is done. The sacks go on walking, a few at a time, for the rest of the year. Samuel counts them out loud at supper."}]}, "zulu+estrada": {"title": "Short in the Stores", "text": "Things are walking out of the stores Samuel keeps: a sack of seed, then a coil of cable, then another sack. Samuel has started sleeping in there, which isn't helping anything.\n\nToby has come to you with it, in order.\n\n[[zulu]] \"First, the tally is short again. Second, the lock hasn't been forced. Third, with respect, I'd ask to sit up in the stores myself with the lamp out. I won't set any of mine on a guess, and I won't have them watching their own friends.\"\n\n[[estrada]] \"Or.\" \"we ask at supper. Whoever it is, they're hungry or they're frightened. Either way they'll come and say.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Toby's watch", "ok": "Toby sits two nights in the dark between the seed racks. On the third a young technician comes in with an empty sack, and Toby lets it fill before he steps out, because he wants the reason before the name. The seed was traded for cigarettes nobody should still have. Toby reports it to you in order and asks that nobody go to the brig, and Samuel, who has been sitting in the corridor the whole time, takes the technician onto his crew instead.", "bad": "Toby sits the stores door for a week and nobody comes, and Samuel's crews have to wait on him to be let in for their own tools. The thief takes another sack the first night there's nobody on it. Toby apologises to Samuel in front of the whole table and means every word, and Samuel's crews still don't speak to the security detail for a month."}, {"label": "Samuel's way: ask at supper", "info": [["people", "Samuel"], ["danger", "Toby's watch"], ["danger", "A week of waiting"]], "out": "Nobody comes forward for a week. Then a young technician does, in tears, and the seed comes back. Toby answers very correctly.\n\n[[zulu]] \"Understood.\"\n\nHe says nothing else for the rest of supper, and he's at the stores door the next night anyway, to be sure."}, {"label": "Let it go. It's seed", "info": [["danger", "The stores"], ["danger", "Both of them"]], "out": "Nothing is done. The sacks go on walking, a few at a time, for the rest of the year. Samuel counts them out loud at supper, and Toby writes every one into the watch log under his own name."}]}, "dahl+waititi": {"title": "Short in the Stores", "text": "Things are walking out of the stores Hamond keeps: a sack of seed, then a coil of cable, then another sack. Hamond has taken to joking about it at supper, loudly, and to taking the smallest bowl at the table, which isn't helping anything.\n\nNolan has an idea, and is enjoying it.\n\n[[dahl]] \"Leave a sack of the good stuff out and dust the inside with dye, and whoever it is glows green for a week, and then we have a chat, and I'll be very civil about it.\"\n\nHamond shakes his ladle at you.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Don't let him dye anybody, my friend! Whoever it is, they're hungry or they've got somebody to feed. Leave the door open and a pot on at the back of the stores, and they'll come and tell me, because people always do. Ha! I can't keep it to myself after, mind, so you'll all hear.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Nolan's trap", "ok": "It takes four days. A young technician comes on shift with green hands and a story about a rail, and the seed is under a bunk, traded for cigarettes nobody should still have. Nolan has the chat. Hamond sits in on it with a bowl, telling everyone the same thing.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Sit, sit.\"\n\nThe technician ends up on Hamond's kitchen crew instead of in the brig.", "bad": "Half the bay crew handle the sack on the first morning, on honest business, and come up green to the elbow. The real thief never touches it. Hamond laughs it off at supper, a whole crew gone green, ha, and then goes plain and says his people won't be lined up and looked at again. They don't speak to Nolan's detail for a month."}, {"label": "Hamond's way: a pot in the stores", "info": [["people", "Hamond"], ["danger", "Nolan's fun"], ["danger", "A week of waiting"]], "out": "Nobody comes for the pot, and Hamond eats it himself, slowly, and calls it a waste of a good leek. Then a young technician turns up with the seed and an empty bowl, in tears, and Hamond feeds first and asks after. Nolan calls it the least interesting solution in the history of the species, and doesn't take a bowl."}, {"label": "Let it go. It's seed", "info": [["danger", "The stores"], ["danger", "Both of them"]], "out": "Nothing is done. The sacks go on walking, a few at a time, for the rest of the year. Hamond makes a joke of the count every night at supper, and every night his own bowl is a little smaller. Then one night he stops joking and just says the number."}]}, "zulu+waititi": {"title": "Short in the Stores", "text": "Things are walking out of the stores Hamond keeps: a sack of seed, then a coil of cable, then another sack. Hamond has taken to joking about it at supper, loudly, and to taking the smallest bowl at the table, which isn't helping anything.\n\nToby has come to you with it, in order.\n\n[[zulu]] \"First, the tally is short again. Second, the lock hasn't been forced. Third, with respect, I'd ask to sit up in the stores myself with the lamp out. I won't set any of mine on a guess.\"\n\nHamond shakes his ladle at you.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Sit up all you like, my friend, but leave the door open and a pot on while you do! Whoever it is, they're hungry or they've got somebody to feed, and if they smell stew they'll come and tell me. People always do. Ha! I can't keep it to myself after, mind.\"", "choices": [{"label": "Toby's watch", "ok": "Toby sits two nights in the dark between the seed racks. On the third a young technician comes in with an empty sack, and Toby lets it fill before he steps out, because he wants the reason before the name. The seed was traded for cigarettes nobody should still have. Toby reports it to you in order and asks that nobody go to the brig, and Hamond arrives with a bowl and says it to both of them.\n\n[[waititi]] \"Sit, sit.\"\n\nHamond takes the technician onto his kitchen crew.", "bad": "Toby sits the stores door for a week and nobody comes, and Hamond's crews have to wait on him to be let in for their own tools. The thief takes another sack the first night there's nobody on it. Toby apologises to the whole table, correctly, and Hamond, for once, has no joke, and his crews don't speak to the security detail for a month."}, {"label": "Hamond's way: a pot in the stores", "info": [["people", "Hamond"], ["danger", "Toby's watch"], ["danger", "A week of waiting"]], "out": "Nobody comes for the pot, and Hamond eats it himself and calls it a waste of a good leek. Then a young technician turns up with the seed and an empty bowl, in tears, and Hamond feeds first and asks after. Toby says he'd have liked to watch the door, and says it politely, and eats his stew standing at his post."}, {"label": "Let it go. It's seed", "info": [["danger", "The stores"], ["danger", "Both of them"]], "out": "Nothing is done. The sacks go on walking, a few at a time, for the rest of the year. Hamond makes a joke of the count every night at supper until one night he stops and just says the number, and Toby writes every sack into the watch log under his own name."}]}}
};
